</figure>
<section id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Measure Coverage Degree between Two Subspaces.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> be two linear subspaces of <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dim(A)\leq\dim(B)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">dim</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">dim</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dim(A)\leq\dim(B)</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{A}=[u_{1},...,u_{k_{1}}]\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times k_{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{A}=[u_{1},...,u_{k_{1}}]\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times k_{A}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{B}=[v_{1},...,v_{k_{B}}]\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times k_{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{B}=[v_{1},...,v_{k_{B}}]\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times k_{B}}</annotation></semantics></math> be the matrices consisting of the orthonormal bases of <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively. We define the Coverage Score to quantify the extent to which <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> is contained within <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A3.E19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Coverage Score}(A,B)=\frac{1}{k_{A}}\|P_{A}^{\top}P_{B}\|_{*}=\frac{1}{k_{A}}\sum_{i=1}^{k_{A}}\cos\theta_{i}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>Coverage Score</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></munderover><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Coverage Score}(A,B)=\frac{1}{k_{A}}\|P_{A}^{\top}P_{B}\|_{*}=\frac{1}{k_{A}}\sum_{i=1}^{k_{A}}\cos\theta_{i},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|\cdot\|_{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\cdot\|_{*}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the nuclear norm, and <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> represent
the <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th principal angle between subspaces <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>.
By definition, the Coverage Score lies in the interval <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>. It represents the mean squared norm of the projection of <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>’s basis vectors onto the subspace <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>. A score of <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> indicates that <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\subseteq B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\subseteq B</annotation></semantics></math>, while a score of <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> implies that <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> is orthogonal to <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> (<math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\perp B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⟂</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\perp B</annotation></semantics></math>). A value closer to <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> suggests a higher degree of containment of <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> within <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>Experimental Details in Sections <a href="#S6" title="6 Experiments ‣ Accelerating LLM Pre-Training through Flat-Direction Dynamics Enhancement" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> </h3>

<section id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Muon Baselines.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We adopt the standard Muon configuration described in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al., 2025a</a>)</cite>. Specifically, we apply Muon specifically to 2D matrix blocks within transformer layers, while using AdamW for all other parameters (RMSNorm (<span id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">norm</span>), Embedding (<span id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">emb</span>) and the Output (<span id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">out</span>)). We set the learning rate scaling factor to <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c=0.2\max\{m,n\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>0.2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c=0.2\max\{m,n\}</annotation></semantics></math> for blocks that use Muon with shape <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{m\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{m\times n}</annotation></semantics></math>, ensuring the update RMS norm aligns with that of AdamW. The baseline is configured with Nesterov momentum using a decay coefficient <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{\text{muon}}=0.95" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>muon</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.95</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{\text{muon}}=0.95</annotation></semantics></math>, weight decay <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=0.1</annotation></semantics></math>, and a gradient clipping threshold of <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">SOAP Baselines.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We maintain the same weight decay and gradient clipping settings as in Muon. Following <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">Vyas et al., 2025</a>)</cite>, we set the hyper-parameters to <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta=0.95" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.95</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta=0.95</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{v}=0.99" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.99</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{v}=0.99</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=10</annotation></semantics></math>. regarding the shampoo momentum, although <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">Vyas et al., 2025</a>)</cite> recommends <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{\operatorname{shampoo}}=0.99" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>shampoo</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.99</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{\operatorname{shampoo}}=0.99</annotation></semantics></math>, we compared <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{\operatorname{shampoo}}\in\{0.99,0.95\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>shampoo</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0.99</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.95</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{\operatorname{shampoo}}\in\{0.99,0.95\}</annotation></semantics></math> and selected <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.95" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.95</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.95</annotation></semantics></math>, as it yielded lower validation losses in our experiments.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Learning Rate Schedules.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For the <span id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">cos</span> schedule, following <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hoffmann et al. (2022)</a></cite>, the minimum learning rate <span id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">lr_min</span> is set to <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.1\times\texttt{lr\_max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">lr_max</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.1\times\texttt{lr\_max}</annotation></semantics></math>. For the <span id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">wsd</span> schedule, we allocate the warmup and stable phases to the first <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="80\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>80</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">80\%</annotation></semantics></math> of total iterations, followed by a linear decay to <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> over the remaining <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="20\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>20</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">20\%</annotation></semantics></math>. We set the warm-up steps to <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1000</annotation></semantics></math> for all pre-training experiments.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Additionally,</p>
<ul id="A3.I4" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:2em;">
<li id="A3.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I4.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">C4 pre-training.</span> We use a sequence length of 256 and a global batch size of 3,600. The total number of training tokens is set to approximately 80 times the number of model parameters, corresponding to <math id="A3.I4.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="4\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4\times</annotation></semantics></math> the Chinchilla scaling law <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hoffmann et al., 2022</a>)</cite>. The training process includes 1,000 warm-up steps. We perform a grid search for the maximum learning rate <span id="A3.I4.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">lr_max</span> over the set <math id="A3.I4.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\texttt{1e-3},\texttt{2e-3},\texttt{3e-3},\texttt{5e-3},\texttt{7e-3}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">1e-3</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">2e-3</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">3e-3</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">5e-3</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">7e-3</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\texttt{1e-3},\texttt{2e-3},\texttt{3e-3},\texttt{5e-3},\texttt{7e-3}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. The resulting optimal learning rates for each model are detailed in Table <a href="#A3.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ Appendix C Experimental Details ‣ Accelerating LLM Pre-Training through Flat-Direction Dynamics Enhancement" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I4.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Pile pre-training.</span> We set the sequence length to 1,024. The batch size is set to 1,024 for the 0.25B and 0.5B models, and 2,048 for the 1.3B model. The total number of training tokens is approximately 40 times the number of model parameters (corresponding to <math id="A3.I4.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="4\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4\times</annotation></semantics></math> the Chinchilla scaling law <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hoffmann et al., 2022</a>)</cite>), which includes 1,000 warm-up steps. A grid search for <span id="A3.I4.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">lr_max</span> is performed over the set <math id="A3.I4.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\texttt{7e-4},\texttt{1e-3},\texttt{2e-3},\texttt{3e-3},\texttt{5e-3},\texttt{7e-3}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">7e-4</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">1e-3</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">2e-3</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">3e-3</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">5e-3</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">7e-3</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\texttt{7e-4},\texttt{1e-3},\texttt{2e-3},\texttt{3e-3},\texttt{5e-3},\texttt{7e-3}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. The optimal learning rates for each model are detailed in <a href="#A3.T2" title="In Appendix C Experimental Details ‣ Accelerating LLM Pre-Training through Flat-Direction Dynamics Enhancement" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Tables</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> and <a href="#A3.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ Appendix C Experimental Details ‣ Accelerating LLM Pre-Training through Flat-Direction Dynamics Enhancement" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Hyper-parameter tuning for <span id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Muon-LITE</span>.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For LLaMA models, we identified the optimal hyper-parameters <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\chi,\beta_{1},\beta_{2}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>χ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\chi,\beta_{1},\beta_{2}\}</annotation></semantics></math> via grid search on the 250M model (Pile) and applied them uniformly to the 130M (C4), 500M (Pile), and 1.3B (Pile) experiments. Specifically, fixing the base learning rate to Muon’s optimal value, we searched the sharp subspace dimension ration <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{s}\in\{0.1,0.2\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0.1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{s}\in\{0.1,0.2\}</annotation></semantics></math>, and set <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{s}=r_{s}\min\{m,n\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{s}=r_{s}\min\{m,n\}</annotation></semantics></math> for <span id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">q,k,v,o,ffn</span> blocks of size <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{m\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{m\times n}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{s}=r_{s}mn" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{s}=r_{s}mn</annotation></semantics></math> for <span id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">emb, norm</span> blocks, with all of them using the same ratio <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{s}</annotation></semantics></math>. The search space for other coefficients is <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{1}\in\{0.0,-0.25\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0.0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.25</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{1}\in\{0.0,-0.25\}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{2}\in\{0.5,1.0,2.0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0.5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1.0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2.0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{2}\in\{0.5,1.0,2.0\}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi\in\{2.0,4.0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>χ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>2.0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4.0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi\in\{2.0,4.0\}</annotation></semantics></math>. For AdamW blocks, we set <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{1,2}=0.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{1,2}=0.0</annotation></semantics></math> for brevity, and <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\operatorname{smooth}}=0.1mn" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>smooth</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>0.1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\operatorname{smooth}}=0.1mn</annotation></semantics></math> (the final loss is insensitive to this parameter). Following <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al., 2025a</a>)</cite>, we exclude the <span id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">output</span> block from <span id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">LITE</span> (<em id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.1.5" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">i.e.</em> treating the entire block as sharp directions), as accelerating it offers minimal gains and may risk instability. Finally, we selected <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{s}=0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{s}=0.1</annotation></semantics></math> and the specific settings in <span id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">LITE</span> variants for LLaMA models are:</p>
<ul id="A3.I5" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A3.I5.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I5.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I5.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I5.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Muon-LITE</span>-H: <math id="A3.I5.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\beta_{1},\beta_{2})=(-0.25,2.0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.25</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2.0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\beta_{1},\beta_{2})=(-0.25,2.0)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I5.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I5.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I5.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I5.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Muon-LITE</span>-L: <math id="A3.I5.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>χ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi=4</annotation></semantics></math> for <span id="A3.I5.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">emb, norm</span> blocks and <math id="A3.I5.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>χ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi=2</annotation></semantics></math> for Muon blocks.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I5.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I5.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I5.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I5.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Muon-LITE</span>: Adopts the <math id="A3.I5.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>χ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi</annotation></semantics></math> settings from <span id="A3.I5.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Muon-LITE</span>-L and sets <math id="A3.I5.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\beta_{1},\beta_{2})=(-0.25,1.0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.25</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1.0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\beta_{1},\beta_{2})=(-0.25,1.0)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For <span id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Muon-LITE</span> in the QwenMoE experiment, we set <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{s}=0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{s}=0.1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{1}=0.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{1}=0.0</annotation></semantics></math>. We searched <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi\in\{4,8\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>χ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi\in\{4,8\}</annotation></semantics></math> for <span id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">emb</span> and <span id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">norm</span> blocks (while maintaining <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>χ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi=1</annotation></semantics></math> for others) and <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{2}\in\{1.0,2.0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1.0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2.0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{2}\in\{1.0,2.0\}</annotation></semantics></math> for blocks using Muon. The final configuration adopted was <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi=8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>χ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi=8</annotation></semantics></math> (for <span id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">emb</span>/<span id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p2.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">norm</span>) and <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{2}=1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{2}=1.0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Hyper-parameter tuning for <span id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">SOAP-LITE</span>.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Similar to <span id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Muon-LITE</span>. we identified the optimal hyper-parameters <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\chi,\beta_{1},\beta_{2}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>χ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\chi,\beta_{1},\beta_{2}\}</annotation></semantics></math> via grid search on the 250M model (Pile) and applied them to other scenarios. Specifically, fixing the base learning rate to SOAP’s optimal value, we searched the sharp subspace dimension ration <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{s}\in\{0.1,0.2\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0.1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{s}\in\{0.1,0.2\}</annotation></semantics></math>, and set <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{s}=r_{s}mn" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{s}=r_{s}mn</annotation></semantics></math> for all blocks, with all of them using the same ratio <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{s}</annotation></semantics></math>. The search space for other coefficients is <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{1}=0.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{1}=0.0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{2}\in\{0.25,0.5,1.0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0.25</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1.0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{2}\in\{0.25,0.5,1.0\}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi\in\{2.0,4.0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>χ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>2.0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4.0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi\in\{2.0,4.0\}</annotation></semantics></math>. We set <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\operatorname{smooth}}=0.1mn" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>smooth</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>0.1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\operatorname{smooth}}=0.1mn</annotation></semantics></math> uniformly (the final loss is insensitive to this parameter). Following <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al., 2025a</a>)</cite>, we exclude the <span id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">output</span> block from <span id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">LITE</span> (<em id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.1.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">i.e.</em> treating the entire block as sharp directions), as accelerating it offers minimal gains and may risk instability. Finally, we selected <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{s}=0.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{s}=0.2</annotation></semantics></math> and the specific settings in <span id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">SOAP-LITE</span> variants for LLaMA models are:</p>
<ul id="A3.I6" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A3.I6.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I6.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I6.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I6.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">SOAP-LITE</span>-H: <math id="A3.I6.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\beta_{1},\beta_{2})=(0.0,0.5)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0.0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.5</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\beta_{1},\beta_{2})=(0.0,0.5)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I6.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I6.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I6.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I6.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">SOAP-LITE</span>-L: <math id="A3.I6.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>χ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi=4</annotation></semantics></math> for <span id="A3.I6.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">emb, norm</span> blocks and <math id="A3.I6.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>χ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi=2</annotation></semantics></math> for Muon blocks.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I6.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I6.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I6.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I6.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">SOAP-LITE</span>: Adopts the <math id="A3.I6.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>χ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi</annotation></semantics></math> settings from <span id="A3.I6.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">SOAP-LITE</span>-L and sets <math id="A3.I6.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\beta_{1},\beta_{2})=(0.0,0.25)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0.0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.25</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\beta_{1},\beta_{2})=(0.0,0.25)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Additional Experimental Results</h2>

<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.1 </span>Dense Models</h3>

<div id="A4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Here we present the supplementary results for the experiments in <a href="#S6.SS1" title="6.1 Results on Dense Models ‣ 6 Experiments ‣ Accelerating LLM Pre-Training through Flat-Direction Dynamics Enhancement" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate the 0-shot performance of the pre-trained LLaMA 1.3B models for 25k steps (<a href="#S6.F4" title="In 6.1 Results on Dense Models ‣ 6 Experiments ‣ Accelerating LLM Pre-Training through Flat-Direction Dynamics Enhancement" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>) in <a href="#A4.T4" title="In D.1 Dense Models ‣ Appendix D Additional Experimental Results ‣ Accelerating LLM Pre-Training through Flat-Direction Dynamics Enhancement" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>. <span id="A4.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Muon-LITE</span> demonstrates consistent improvements over the Muon baseline across the eight evaluated tasks. Notably, <span id="A4.SS1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Muon-LITE</span> achieves a substantial gain on BoolQ and exhibits strong generalization on reasoning-heavy benchmarks, showing significant margins on ARC-Challenge (+1.79) and MMLU (+1.39). These results indicate that MUON-LITE effectively enhances model performance across diverse domains ranging from common sense reasoning to truthful QA.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.T4" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A4.T4.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 4</span>: </span><span id="A4.T4.8" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Evaluation results on downstream tasks (0-shot with lm-evaluation-harness) of LLaMA models (1.3B) pre-trained on Pile using <span id="A4.T4.8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Muon-LITE</span> and Muon. The best scores in each column are bolded. Abbreviations: <span id="A4.T4.8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">T_mc2</span>=<span id="A4.T4.8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">TruthfulQA_mc2</span>, <span id="A4.T4.8.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">AVG</span>=Average score.
</span></figcaption>
