<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Discussions on Momentum Formulations and their Continuous-Time ODE Counterparts</h2>

<section id="A5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.1 </span>Continuous-Time ODE Formulations</h3>

<div id="A5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this subsection, we introduce the continuous-time limits of momentum-based algorithms and demonstrate how to derive discrete optimizers from these continuous formulations (modeled as second-order or first-order systems). The derivation proceeds by reducing the second-order dynamics into a first-order system, followed by numerical discretization. This pipeline serves as a foundation for the Riemannian setting (<a href="#S4.E3" title="Equation 3 ‣ Continuous-time Viewpoint. ‣ 4.2 The Riemannian ODE Framework ‣ 4 A Unified Riemannian ODE Framework for Understanding Adaptive Algorithms ‣ Accelerating LLM Pre-Training through Flat-Direction Dynamics Enhancement" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>), which is the primary focus of this work (see Appendix <a href="#A7" title="Appendix G Transforming the Second Order RISHD (the Riemannian ODE Framework) into a First Order System ‣ Accelerating LLM Pre-Training through Flat-Direction Dynamics Enhancement" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G</span></a>). We consider the inertial system with Hessian damping (ISHD) mentioned in <a href="#S3.SS2" title="3.2 ODE Perspective of Momentum-based Algorithms ‣ 3 Preliminary ‣ Accelerating LLM Pre-Training through Flat-Direction Dynamics Enhancement" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a></p>
<table id="A5.E20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E20.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\ddot{w}_{t}+\alpha_{t}\dot{w}_{t}+\beta_{t}\nabla^{2}f(w_{t})\dot{w}_{t}+\gamma_{t}\nabla f(w_{t})=0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>¨</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ddot{w}_{t}+\alpha_{t}\dot{w}_{t}+\beta_{t}\nabla^{2}f(w_{t})\dot{w}_{t}+\gamma_{t}\nabla f(w_{t})=0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t},\beta_{t},\gamma_{t}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t},\beta_{t},\gamma_{t}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> denote the coefficients for momentum decay, Hessian damping, and the gradient driving force, respectively. By introducing an auxiliary momentum variable <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> to track the velocity <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{w}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{w}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, we can reformulate this second-order equation (<a href="#A5.E20" title="Equation 20 ‣ E.1 Continuous-Time ODE Formulations ‣ Appendix E Discussions on Momentum Formulations and their Continuous-Time ODE Counterparts ‣ Accelerating LLM Pre-Training through Flat-Direction Dynamics Enhancement" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a>) into an equivalent first-order system:</p>
<table id="A5.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{cases}\dot{w}_{t}=-\gamma_{t}m_{t}-\beta_{t}\nabla f(w_{t}),\\
\dot{m}_{t}=-\alpha_{t}m_{t}+(1-{\alpha_{t}\beta_{t}}/{\gamma_{t}}-\dot{\beta}_{t})\nabla f(w_{t}).\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>γ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mi>m</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>m</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>α</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mi>m</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mi>β</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>γ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{cases}\dot{w}_{t}=-\gamma_{t}m_{t}-\beta_{t}\nabla f(w_{t}),\\
\dot{m}_{t}=-\alpha_{t}m_{t}+(1-{\alpha_{t}\beta_{t}}/{\gamma_{t}}-\dot{\beta}_{t})\nabla f(w_{t}).\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Applying a discretization with step size <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> yields the following update rule at the <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-th iteration:</p>
<table id="A5.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{cases}m_{k}=(1-\alpha_{t}h)m_{k-1}+(1-{\alpha_{k}\beta_{k}}/{\gamma_{k}}-\dot{\beta}_{k})h\nabla f(w_{k}),\\
w_{k+1}=w_{k}-\gamma_{k}hm_{k}-\beta_{k}h\nabla f(w_{k}).\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>m</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>m</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mi>β</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>γ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mi>h</mi><mi>m</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{cases}m_{k}=(1-\alpha_{t}h)m_{k-1}+(1-{\alpha_{k}\beta_{k}}/{\gamma_{k}}-\dot{\beta}_{k})h\nabla f(w_{k}),\\
w_{k+1}=w_{k}-\gamma_{k}hm_{k}-\beta_{k}h\nabla f(w_{k}).\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">This formulation subsumes various momentum methods, recovering Heavy Ball momentum when <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{k}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{k}=0</annotation></semantics></math> and Nesterov-type momentum when <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{k}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{k}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. Crucially, the Hessian damping term <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{t}\nabla^{2}f(w_{t})\dot{w}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{t}\nabla^{2}f(w_{t})\dot{w}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and its discretized counterpart <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\beta_{k}\nabla f(w_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{k}\nabla f(w_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> serves to enhance standard Heavy Ball momentum by suppressing oscillations. We provide a detailed discussion in Appendix <a href="#A5.SS2" title="E.2 Heavy Ball Momentum, Nesterov Momentum, and Hessian Damping ‣ Appendix E Discussions on Momentum Formulations and their Continuous-Time ODE Counterparts ‣ Accelerating LLM Pre-Training through Flat-Direction Dynamics Enhancement" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.2 </span>Heavy Ball Momentum, Nesterov Momentum, and Hessian Damping</h3>

<div id="A5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we discuss equivalent formulations of Nesterov-type momentum and Heavy Ball momentum (also known as Polyak momentum). Furthermore, we analyze the acceleration dynamics of Nesterov momentum, highlighting the intrinsic connections between <span id="A5.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Hessian damping and gradient correction.</span>
For brevity, we assume the preconditioner is the identity matrix (<math id="A5.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F=I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F=I</annotation></semantics></math>) throughout this discussion.</p>
</div>
<section id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Heavy Ball Momentum.</h4>

<div id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The Heavy Ball momentum update is defined as:</p>
<table id="A5.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{cases}m_{k}=(1-\alpha)m_{k-1}+\nabla f(w_{k}),\\
w_{k+1}=w_{k}-\eta m_{k}.\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{cases}m_{k}=(1-\alpha)m_{k-1}+\nabla f(w_{k}),\\
w_{k+1}=w_{k}-\eta m_{k}.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">This recurrence can be rewritten in a single-variable form equivalent to:</p>
<table id="A5.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E24.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle w_{k+1}=w_{k}+(1-\alpha)(w_{k}-w_{k-1})-\eta\nabla f\left(w_{k}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle w_{k+1}=w_{k}+(1-\alpha)(w_{k}-w_{k-1})-\eta\nabla f\left(w_{k}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">This formulation aligns with the momentum schemes adopted in AdamW and many other adaptive optimizers. Note that here, the coefficient <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> of the gradient term (typical in EMA-style updates) is absorbed into the effective learning rate <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Nesterov Momentum.</h4>

<div id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Unfortunately, Heavy Ball momentum lacks a theoretical guarantee of globally achieving a faster convergence rate than Gradient Descent, even in deterministic strongly convex settings. In contrast, Nesterov momentum provably achieves acceleration: the convergence rates for Gradient Descent and Nesterov momentum are approximately <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-\frac{1}{\kappa})^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>κ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-\frac{1}{\kappa})^{k}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-\frac{1}{\sqrt{\kappa}})^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi>κ</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-\frac{1}{\sqrt{\kappa}})^{k}</annotation></semantics></math> respectively, where <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the condition number.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.3" class="ltx_p">Nesterov momentum with constant coefficients is typically formulated as:</p>
<table id="A5.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{cases}x_{k}=w_{k-1}-\eta\nabla f(w_{k-1}),\\
w_{k}=x_{k}+(1-\alpha)(x_{k}-x_{k-1}).\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{cases}x_{k}=w_{k-1}-\eta\nabla f(w_{k-1}),\\
w_{k}=x_{k}+(1-\alpha)(x_{k}-x_{k-1}).\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.4" class="ltx_p">Eliminating the auxiliary variable <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> yields two equivalent interpretations of (<a href="#A5.E25" title="Equation 25 ‣ Nesterov Momentum. ‣ E.2 Heavy Ball Momentum, Nesterov Momentum, and Hessian Damping ‣ Appendix E Discussions on Momentum Formulations and their Continuous-Time ODE Counterparts ‣ Accelerating LLM Pre-Training through Flat-Direction Dynamics Enhancement" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">25</span></a>):</p>
<table id="A5.E26" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A5.E26X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E26X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle x_{k+1}=x_{k}+(1-\alpha)(x_{k}-x_{k-1})-\eta\underbrace{\nabla f\left(x_{k}+(1-\alpha)(x_{k}-x_{k-1})\right)}_{\text{gradient correction}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>gradient correction</mtext></munder></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle x_{k+1}=x_{k}+(1-\alpha)(x_{k}-x_{k-1})-\eta\underbrace{\nabla f\left(x_{k}+(1-\alpha)(x_{k}-x_{k-1})\right)}_{\text{gradient correction}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.5" class="ltx_p">and</p>
<table id="A5.E27" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A5.E27X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E27X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle w_{k+1}=w_{k}+(1-\alpha)(w_{k}-w_{k-1})-\eta\nabla f\left(w_{k}\right)-(1-\alpha)\eta\underbrace{(\nabla f(w_{k})-\nabla f(w_{k-1}))}_{\text{gradient correction}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>)</mo><mo>−</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>η</mi><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>gradient correction</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle w_{k+1}=w_{k}+(1-\alpha)(w_{k}-w_{k-1})-\eta\nabla f\left(w_{k}\right)-(1-\alpha)\eta\underbrace{(\nabla f(w_{k})-\nabla f(w_{k-1}))}_{\text{gradient correction}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">The Gradient Correction (Hessian Damping) Insight.</h4>

<div id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Comparing (<a href="#A5.E27" title="Equation 27 ‣ Nesterov Momentum. ‣ E.2 Heavy Ball Momentum, Nesterov Momentum, and Hessian Damping ‣ Appendix E Discussions on Momentum Formulations and their Continuous-Time ODE Counterparts ‣ Accelerating LLM Pre-Training through Flat-Direction Dynamics Enhancement" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">27</span></a>) with the Heavy Ball form (<a href="#A5.E24" title="Equation 24 ‣ Heavy Ball Momentum. ‣ E.2 Heavy Ball Momentum, Nesterov Momentum, and Hessian Damping ‣ Appendix E Discussions on Momentum Formulations and their Continuous-Time ODE Counterparts ‣ Accelerating LLM Pre-Training through Flat-Direction Dynamics Enhancement" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24</span></a>), it is evident that Nesterov momentum introduces an additional <span id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">gradient correction term</span>. Using a Taylor expansion, we observe that:</p>
<table id="A5.E28" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A5.E28X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E28X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla f(x_{k}+(1-\alpha)(x_{k}-x_{k-1}))\approx(1-\alpha)\nabla^{2}f(x_{k})(x_{k}-x_{k-1})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla f(x_{k}+(1-\alpha)(x_{k}-x_{k-1}))\approx(1-\alpha)\nabla^{2}f(x_{k})(x_{k}-x_{k-1}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.E28Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E28Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla f(w_{k})-\nabla f(w_{k-1})\approx\nabla^{2}f(w_{k})(w_{k}-w_{k-1})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla f(w_{k})-\nabla f(w_{k-1})\approx\nabla^{2}f(w_{k})(w_{k}-w_{k-1}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">This reveals that the gradient correction implicitly incorporates <span id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Hessian information</span>. This mechanism is the key to the acceleration of Nesterov momentum: it exerts an inertial damping effect (often referred to as Hessian damping) which is proportional to the curvature. Consequently, this term applies stronger damping in directions corresponding to large Hessian eigenvalues, effectively suppressing oscillations.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">The formulation in (<a href="#A5.E27" title="Equation 27 ‣ Nesterov Momentum. ‣ E.2 Heavy Ball Momentum, Nesterov Momentum, and Hessian Damping ‣ Appendix E Discussions on Momentum Formulations and their Continuous-Time ODE Counterparts ‣ Accelerating LLM Pre-Training through Flat-Direction Dynamics Enhancement" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">27</span></a>) is also mathematically equivalent to:</p>
<table id="A5.E29" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A5.E29X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E29X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle w_{k+1}=w_{k}+(1-\alpha)(w_{k}-w_{k-1})-\eta_{1}(1+\alpha\beta)\nabla f\left(w_{k}\right)-\beta\eta_{1}(1-\alpha)\underbrace{(\nabla f(w_{k})-\nabla f(w_{k-1}))}_{\text{gradient correction}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi><mi>β</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>η</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>gradient correction</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle w_{k+1}=w_{k}+(1-\alpha)(w_{k}-w_{k-1})-\eta_{1}(1+\alpha\beta)\nabla f\left(w_{k}\right)-\beta\eta_{1}(1-\alpha)\underbrace{(\nabla f(w_{k})-\nabla f(w_{k-1}))}_{\text{gradient correction}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.3" class="ltx_p">with <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{1}=\eta/(1+\alpha\beta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{1}=\eta/(1+\alpha\beta)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=1/(1-\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=1/(1-\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math>. Note that (<a href="#A5.E29" title="Equation 29 ‣ The Gradient Correction (Hessian Damping) Insight. ‣ E.2 Heavy Ball Momentum, Nesterov Momentum, and Hessian Damping ‣ Appendix E Discussions on Momentum Formulations and their Continuous-Time ODE Counterparts ‣ Accelerating LLM Pre-Training through Flat-Direction Dynamics Enhancement" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">29</span></a>) can be transformed as:</p>
<table id="A5.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{cases}m_{k}=(1-\alpha)m_{k-1}+\nabla f(w_{k}),\\
w_{k+1}=w_{k}-\eta_{1}(m_{k}+\beta\nabla f(w_{k})),\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{cases}m_{k}=(1-\alpha)m_{k-1}+\nabla f(w_{k}),\\
w_{k+1}=w_{k}-\eta_{1}(m_{k}+\beta\nabla f(w_{k})),\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.4" class="ltx_p">which corresponds to the discretized form discussed in Section <a href="#S3.SS2" title="3.2 ODE Perspective of Momentum-based Algorithms ‣ 3 Preliminary ‣ Accelerating LLM Pre-Training through Flat-Direction Dynamics Enhancement" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We can observe that the term <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\beta\nabla f(w_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\nabla f(w_{k})</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#A5.E30" title="Equation 30 ‣ The Gradient Correction (Hessian Damping) Insight. ‣ E.2 Heavy Ball Momentum, Nesterov Momentum, and Hessian Damping ‣ Appendix E Discussions on Momentum Formulations and their Continuous-Time ODE Counterparts ‣ Accelerating LLM Pre-Training through Flat-Direction Dynamics Enhancement" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">30</span></a>) (<em id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">i.e.</em> the gradient correction term in (<a href="#A5.E29" title="Equation 29 ‣ The Gradient Correction (Hessian Damping) Insight. ‣ E.2 Heavy Ball Momentum, Nesterov Momentum, and Hessian Damping ‣ Appendix E Discussions on Momentum Formulations and their Continuous-Time ODE Counterparts ‣ Accelerating LLM Pre-Training through Flat-Direction Dynamics Enhancement" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">29</span></a>)) arises from discretizing the Hessian damping term <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\nabla^{2}f(w_{t})\dot{w}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\nabla^{2}f(w_{t})\dot{w}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> in Eq. (<a href="#S3.E1" title="Equation 1 ‣ 3.2 ODE Perspective of Momentum-based Algorithms ‣ 3 Preliminary ‣ Accelerating LLM Pre-Training through Flat-Direction Dynamics Enhancement" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">These insights lead to two key conclusions:</p>
<ol id="A5.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A5.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Implicit Hessian Awareness:</span> Compared with Heavy ball momentum, Nesterov momentum introduces an additional gradient correction term that implicitly encapsulates Hessian information (<em id="A5.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">i.e.</em> Hessian damping), which is instrumental in achieving acceleration.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Continuous-Discrete Correspondence:</span> This gradient correction term naturally arises from the discretization of the Hessian damping term found in the continuous-time limiting flow.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Further Improving Nesterov momentum</h4>

<div id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Although Nesterov momentum leverages Hessian damping (via gradient correction) to achieve acceleration, the coefficient <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> of this term is rigidly constrained by the momentum parameter (<em id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">i.e.</em> <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=1/(1-\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=1/(1-\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math>). It is therefore natural to relax this constraint and search for an optimal <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>, a direction supported by recent theoretical results <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">Attouch et al., 2022</a>; <a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">Xie et al., 2025</a>)</cite>. In this work, we adopt this generalized perspective and incorporate richer second-order information, employing a larger <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> in flat directions than in sharp directions to further enhance acceleration.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.3 </span>Modeling AdEMAMix via a Third-Order ODE</h3>

<div id="A5.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The AdEMAMix optimizer <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">Pagliardini et al., 2025</a>)</cite> builds upon the paradigm of AdamW by incorporating an additional “slow” momentum term. At the <math id="A5.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-th iteration, the parameter update rule is given by:</p>
<table id="A5.E31" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A5.E31X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E31X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle m_{k}^{\mathrm{fast}}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>fast</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle m_{k}^{\mathrm{fast}}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E31X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(1-\alpha_{1})m_{k-1}^{\mathrm{fast}}+\alpha_{1}g_{k}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>fast</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(1-\alpha_{1})m_{k-1}^{\mathrm{fast}}+\alpha_{1}g_{k},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="4" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(31)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.E31Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E31Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle m_{k}^{\mathrm{slow}}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>slow</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle m_{k}^{\mathrm{slow}}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E31Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(1-\alpha_{2})m_{k-1}^{\mathrm{slow}}+\alpha_{2}g_{k}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>slow</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(1-\alpha_{2})m_{k-1}^{\mathrm{slow}}+\alpha_{2}g_{k},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.E31Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E31Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle v_{k}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle v_{k}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E31Xb.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(1-\beta_{\mathrm{adam}})v_{k-1}+\beta_{\mathrm{adam}}g_{k}^{\odot 2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>adam</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>adam</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(1-\beta_{\mathrm{adam}})v_{k-1}+\beta_{\mathrm{adam}}g_{k}^{\odot 2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.E31Xc" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E31Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle w_{k+1}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle w_{k+1}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E31Xc.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle w_{k}-\eta_{k}\frac{m_{k}^{\mathrm{fast}}+\kappa m_{k}^{\mathrm{slow}}}{v_{k}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>fast</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>slow</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle w_{k}-\eta_{k}\frac{m_{k}^{\mathrm{fast}}+\kappa m_{k}^{\mathrm{slow}}}{v_{k}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A5.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the stochastic gradient. For brevity, we omit the weight decay and assume constant momentum hyper-parameters. Typically, <math id="A5.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is set to approximately <math id="A5.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.1</annotation></semantics></math>, while <math id="A5.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> takes much smaller values, such as <math id="A5.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10^{-4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10^{-4}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">To derive its continuous-time version, we first simplify the analysis by omitting the preconditioner <math id="A5.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> and treating the learning rate <math id="A5.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> as a constant <math id="A5.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math>. This yields the following system of differential equations:</p>
<table id="A5.E32" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A5.E32X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E32X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{d}{dt}m_{t}^{\mathrm{fast}}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>fast</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{d}{dt}m_{t}^{\mathrm{fast}}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E32X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\alpha_{1}m_{k-1}^{\mathrm{fast}}+\alpha_{1}\nabla f(w_{k})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>m</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>fast</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\alpha_{1}m_{k-1}^{\mathrm{fast}}+\alpha_{1}\nabla f(w_{k}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="3" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(32)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.E32Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E32Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{d}{dt}m_{t}^{\mathrm{slow}}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>slow</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{d}{dt}m_{t}^{\mathrm{slow}}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E32Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\alpha_{2}m_{k-1}^{\mathrm{slow}}+\alpha_{2}\nabla f(w_{k})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>m</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>slow</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\alpha_{2}m_{k-1}^{\mathrm{slow}}+\alpha_{2}\nabla f(w_{k}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.E32Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E32Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{d}{dt}w_{t}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{d}{dt}w_{t}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E32Xb.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\eta(m_{t}^{\mathrm{fast}}+\kappa m_{t}^{\mathrm{slow}})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>fast</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>slow</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\eta(m_{t}^{\mathrm{fast}}+\kappa m_{t}^{\mathrm{slow}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS3.p2.3" class="ltx_p">We note that applying a discretization with step size <math id="A5.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h=1</annotation></semantics></math> to the above system recovers the update rules in (<a href="#A5.E31" title="Equation 31 ‣ E.3 Modeling AdEMAMix via a Third-Order ODE ‣ Appendix E Discussions on Momentum Formulations and their Continuous-Time ODE Counterparts ‣ Accelerating LLM Pre-Training through Flat-Direction Dynamics Enhancement" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">31</span></a>). Next, we compute the second and third-order time derivatives of the parameters, <math id="A5.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{d^{2}}{dt^{2}}w_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d^{2}}{dt^{2}}w_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{d^{3}}{dt^{3}}w_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d^{3}}{dt^{3}}w_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A5.E33" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A5.E33X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E33X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{d^{2}}{dt^{2}}w_{t}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{d^{2}}{dt^{2}}w_{t}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E33X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\eta(-\alpha_{1}m_{t}^{\mathrm{fast}}-\alpha_{2}\kappa m_{t}^{\mathrm{slow}}+(\alpha_{1}+\kappa\alpha_{2})\nabla f(w_{t}))," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>α</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>m</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>fast</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>m</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>slow</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>κ</mi><mi>α</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\eta(-\alpha_{1}m_{t}^{\mathrm{fast}}-\alpha_{2}\kappa m_{t}^{\mathrm{slow}}+(\alpha_{1}+\kappa\alpha_{2})\nabla f(w_{t})),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(33)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.E33Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E33Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{d^{3}}{dt^{3}}w_{t}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{d^{3}}{dt^{3}}w_{t}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E33Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\eta(\alpha_{1}^{2}m_{t}^{\mathrm{fast}}+\alpha_{2}^{2}\kappa m_{t}^{\mathrm{slow}}-(\alpha_{1}^{2}+\kappa\alpha_{2}^{2})\nabla f(w_{t})+(\alpha_{1}+\kappa\alpha_{2})\nabla^{2}f(w_{t})\frac{d}{dt}w_{t})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>m</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>fast</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>κ</mi><mi>m</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>slow</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>κ</mi><mi>α</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>κ</mi><mi>α</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\eta(\alpha_{1}^{2}m_{t}^{\mathrm{fast}}+\alpha_{2}^{2}\kappa m_{t}^{\mathrm{slow}}-(\alpha_{1}^{2}+\kappa\alpha_{2}^{2})\nabla f(w_{t})+(\alpha_{1}+\kappa\alpha_{2})\nabla^{2}f(w_{t})\frac{d}{dt}w_{t}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS3.p2.4" class="ltx_p">By combining (<a href="#A5.E33" title="Equation 33 ‣ E.3 Modeling AdEMAMix via a Third-Order ODE ‣ Appendix E Discussions on Momentum Formulations and their Continuous-Time ODE Counterparts ‣ Accelerating LLM Pre-Training through Flat-Direction Dynamics Enhancement" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">33</span></a>) with the velocity equation <math id="A5.SS3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{d}{dt}w_{t}=-\eta(m_{t}^{\mathrm{fast}}+\kappa m_{t}^{\mathrm{slow}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>fast</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>slow</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d}{dt}w_{t}=-\eta(m_{t}^{\mathrm{fast}}+\kappa m_{t}^{\mathrm{slow}})</annotation></semantics></math> to eliminate the momentum variables <math id="A5.SS3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{t}^{\mathrm{fast}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>fast</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{t}^{\mathrm{fast}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS3.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{t}^{\mathrm{slow}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>slow</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{t}^{\mathrm{slow}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we arrive at the following third-order ODE :</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A5.E34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underbrace{\frac{d^{3}}{dt^{3}}w_{t}}_{\text{jerk}}+(\alpha_{1}+\alpha_{2})\underbrace{\frac{d^{2}}{dt^{2}}w_{t}}_{\begin{subarray}{c}\text{accelerated}\\
\text{velocity}\end{subarray}}+\alpha_{1}\alpha_{2}\underbrace{\frac{d}{dt}w_{t}}_{\text{velocity}}+\eta(\alpha_{1}+\kappa\alpha_{2})\underbrace{\nabla^{2}f(w_{t})\frac{d}{dt}w_{t}}_{\text{Hessian damping}}+\eta(1+\alpha_{1}\alpha_{2})\underbrace{\nabla f(w_{t})}_{\text{gradient}}=0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>jerk</mtext></munder><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mtext>accelerated</mtext></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mtext>velocity</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>velocity</mtext></munder></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>Hessian damping</mtext></munder></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>gradient</mtext></munder></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underbrace{\frac{d^{3}}{dt^{3}}w_{t}}_{\text{jerk}}+(\alpha_{1}+\alpha_{2})\underbrace{\frac{d^{2}}{dt^{2}}w_{t}}_{\begin{subarray}{c}\text{accelerated}\\
\text{velocity}\end{subarray}}+\alpha_{1}\alpha_{2}\underbrace{\frac{d}{dt}w_{t}}_{\text{velocity}}+\eta(\alpha_{1}+\kappa\alpha_{2})\underbrace{\nabla^{2}f(w_{t})\frac{d}{dt}w_{t}}_{\text{Hessian damping}}+\eta(1+\alpha_{1}\alpha_{2})\underbrace{\nabla f(w_{t})}_{\text{gradient}}=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(34)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Similar to (<a href="#S4.E3" title="Equation 3 ‣ Continuous-time Viewpoint. ‣ 4.2 The Riemannian ODE Framework ‣ 4 A Unified Riemannian ODE Framework for Understanding Adaptive Algorithms ‣ Accelerating LLM Pre-Training through Flat-Direction Dynamics Enhancement" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>), the Riemannian counterpart of (<a href="#A5.E34" title="Equation 34 ‣ E.3 Modeling AdEMAMix via a Third-Order ODE ‣ Appendix E Discussions on Momentum Formulations and their Continuous-Time ODE Counterparts ‣ Accelerating LLM Pre-Training through Flat-Direction Dynamics Enhancement" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">34</span></a>) can be derived as</p>
<table id="A5.E35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\dot{w}_{t}}\nabla_{\dot{w}_{t}}\dot{w}_{t}+(\alpha_{1}+\alpha_{2})\nabla_{\dot{w}_{t}}\dot{w}_{t}+\alpha_{1}\alpha_{2}\frac{d}{dt}\dot{w}_{t}+\eta(\alpha_{1}+\kappa\alpha_{2})\frac{d}{dt}\operatorname{grad}f(w_{t})+\eta(1+\alpha_{1}\alpha_{2})\operatorname{grad}f(w_{t})=0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><msub><mo lspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>grad</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>grad</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\dot{w}_{t}}\nabla_{\dot{w}_{t}}\dot{w}_{t}+(\alpha_{1}+\alpha_{2})\nabla_{\dot{w}_{t}}\dot{w}_{t}+\alpha_{1}\alpha_{2}\frac{d}{dt}\dot{w}_{t}+\eta(\alpha_{1}+\kappa\alpha_{2})\frac{d}{dt}\operatorname{grad}f(w_{t})+\eta(1+\alpha_{1}\alpha_{2})\operatorname{grad}f(w_{t})=0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(35)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS3.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where we use <math id="A5.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Hess}(w_{t})\dot{w}_{t}=\frac{d}{dt}\operatorname{grad}f(w_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Hess</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>grad</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Hess}(w_{t})\dot{w}_{t}=\frac{d}{dt}\operatorname{grad}f(w_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Intuitive Interpretation.</h4>

<div id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Standard momentum methods (like Heavy Ball) typically correspond to second-order ODEs, describing a particle with mass and friction. In contrast, Eq. (<a href="#A5.E34" title="Equation 34 ‣ E.3 Modeling AdEMAMix via a Third-Order ODE ‣ Appendix E Discussions on Momentum Formulations and their Continuous-Time ODE Counterparts ‣ Accelerating LLM Pre-Training through Flat-Direction Dynamics Enhancement" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">34</span></a>) reveals that AdEMAMix is governed by a <span id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">third-order</span> dynamics. The term <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{d^{3}}{dt^{3}}w_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d^{3}}{dt^{3}}w_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> introduces the concept of “jerk” (rate of change of accelerated velocity <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ddot{w}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>¨</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ddot{w}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>) into the optimization trajectory. The third-order structure with Hessian damping allows the optimizer to regulate not only velocity but also its rate of change across multiple time scales. As a result, transient gradient fluctuations induced by rapidly varying curvature are attenuated before influencing parameter updates, enabling more stable and robust navigation of highly ill-conditioned landscapes.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>Foundations of Riemannian Geometry</h2>

<div id="A6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we provide a detailed introduction to the foundation for Riemannian Geometry of <math id="A6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathbb{R}^{p},F)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathbb{R}^{p},F)</annotation></semantics></math> considered in the main text. The parameter space is the Euclidean space <math id="A6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{p}</annotation></semantics></math>, while the metric is the Riemannian metric induced by the preconditioner <math id="A6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(w)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(w)</annotation></semantics></math>, which is formally denoted as the manifold <math id="A6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}=(\mathbb{R}^{p},F)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}=(\mathbb{R}^{p},F)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A6.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.1 </span>Riemannian Metric</h3>

<div id="A6.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The core structure of our framework is based on Riemannian metric, a smooth matrix-value map <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F:\mathcal{M}=\mathbb{R}^{p}\to\mathbb{S}_{++}^{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msubsup><mi>𝕊</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>+</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F:\mathcal{M}=\mathbb{R}^{p}\to\mathbb{S}_{++}^{p}</annotation></semantics></math> that assigns an inner product to the tangent space <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{w}\mathcal{M}\cong\mathbb{R}^{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><mo>≅</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{w}\mathcal{M}\cong\mathbb{R}^{p}</annotation></semantics></math> at each point <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w\in\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w\in\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math>. For any tangent vectors <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u,v\in T_{w}\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u,v\in T_{w}\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math>, the inner product is defined as <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle u,v\rangle_{F(w)}\coloneqq u^{\top}F(w)v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle u,v\rangle_{F(w)}\coloneqq u^{\top}F(w)v</annotation></semantics></math>.
This metric induces a norm <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|u\|_{F(w)}=\sqrt{\langle u,u\rangle_{F(w)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|u\|_{F(w)}=\sqrt{\langle u,u\rangle_{F(w)}}</annotation></semantics></math> in the tangent space <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{w}\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{w}\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math>, which measures the magnitude of perturbations <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> relative to the local curvature <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(w)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(w)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">While the tangent space <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{w}\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{w}\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math> characterizes velocities or perturbations, its dual, the cotangent space <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{w}^{*}\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mi>w</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{w}^{*}\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math>, consists of differentials that act linearly on these velocities, naturally representing gradients of functions. Formally, <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{w}^{*}\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mi>w</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{w}^{*}\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math> is the dual space of <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{w}\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{w}\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math>, consisting of all linear functionals <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi:T_{w}\mathcal{M}\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi:T_{w}\mathcal{M}\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>. It also holds that <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{w}\mathcal{M}\cong\mathbb{R}^{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><mo>≅</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{w}\mathcal{M}\cong\mathbb{R}^{p}</annotation></semantics></math>. The cotangent space is equipped with the dual norm <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|u\|_{F(w)^{-1}}=\sqrt{u^{\top}F(w)^{-1}u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|u\|_{F(w)^{-1}}=\sqrt{u^{\top}F(w)^{-1}u}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in T^{*}\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in T^{*}\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math>. In particular, the Riemannian metric <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(w)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(w)</annotation></semantics></math> induces a natural isomorphism between the tangent and cotangent spaces:</p>
<table id="A6.E36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(w):T_{w}\mathcal{M}\to T_{w}^{*}\mathcal{M},\quad F(w)^{-1}:T_{w}^{*}\mathcal{M}\to T_{w}\mathcal{M}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mi>w</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mi>w</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(w):T_{w}\mathcal{M}\to T_{w}^{*}\mathcal{M},\quad F(w)^{-1}:T_{w}^{*}\mathcal{M}\to T_{w}\mathcal{M}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(36)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Under this identification, an element <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi\in T_{w}^{*}\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mi>w</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi\in T_{w}^{*}\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math>
acts as a linear functional on the tangent space via the Euclidean inner product <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi(u)=\xi^{\top}u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi(u)=\xi^{\top}u</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in T_{w}\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in T_{w}\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math>. Inner-product structures of <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{w}\mathcal{M},T_{w}^{*}\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mi>w</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{w}\mathcal{M},T_{w}^{*}\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math> and between them are <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle\cdot,\cdot\rangle_{F(w)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle\cdot,\cdot\rangle_{F(w)}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle\cdot,\cdot\rangle_{F(w)^{-1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle\cdot,\cdot\rangle_{F(w)^{-1}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle\cdot,\cdot\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle\cdot,\cdot\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> respectively.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Based on the Riemannian metric, we can define the length of a smooth curve <math id="A6.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma:[0,1]\to\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma:[0,1]\to\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math>. The Riemannian length <math id="A6.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L(\gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L(\gamma)</annotation></semantics></math> is given by integrating the local norm of the velocity vector <math id="A6.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{\gamma}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{\gamma}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A6.E37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L(\gamma)=\int_{0}^{1}\|\dot{\gamma}(t)\|_{F(\gamma(t))}dt=\int_{0}^{1}\sqrt{\dot{\gamma}(t)^{\top}F(\gamma(t))\dot{\gamma}(t)}dt." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L(\gamma)=\int_{0}^{1}\|\dot{\gamma}(t)\|_{F(\gamma(t))}dt=\int_{0}^{1}\sqrt{\dot{\gamma}(t)^{\top}F(\gamma(t))\dot{\gamma}(t)}dt.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(37)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">The Riemannian distance (or geodesic distance) between two points <math id="A6.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x,y\in\mathcal{M}=\mathbb{R}^{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x,y\in\mathcal{M}=\mathbb{R}^{p}</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as the infimum of lengths over all piecewise smooth curves connecting them:</p>
<table id="A6.E38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{F}(x,y)=\inf_{\gamma\in D}{L(\gamma)}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">inf</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{F}(x,y)=\inf_{\gamma\in D}{L(\gamma)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(38)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p3.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A6.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> is the set containing all smooth curves <math id="A6.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> connecting <math id="A6.SS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A6.SS1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma(0)=x,\gamma(1)=y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma(0)=x,\gamma(1)=y</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The distance reduces to the Euclidean metric when <math id="A6.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F=I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F=I</annotation></semantics></math>. Furthermore, when <math id="A6.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math> are sufficiently close locally, we have <math id="A6.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{F}(x,y)\approx\|x-y\|_{F(x)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{F}(x,y)\approx\|x-y\|_{F(x)}</annotation></semantics></math>. The Riemannian gradient <math id="A6.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{grad}f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>grad</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{grad}f</annotation></semantics></math> is an example of vector field.</p>
</div>
<section id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Smooth Vector Fields and the Tangent Bundle.</h4>

<div id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">With the tangent space <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{w}\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{w}\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math> defined at each point, we consider the collection of all tangent vectors across the manifold, known as the tangent bundle, denoted by <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\mathcal{M}\coloneqq\bigcup_{w\in\mathcal{M}}(\{w\}\times T_{w}\mathcal{M})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≔</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">⋃</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>w</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\mathcal{M}\coloneqq\bigcup_{w\in\mathcal{M}}(\{w\}\times T_{w}\mathcal{M})</annotation></semantics></math>. The tangent bundle is itself a smooth manifold of dimension <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2p</annotation></semantics></math>. A vector field <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math> is a mapping (formally called a <span id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">section</span>) that assigns to every point <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w\in\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w\in\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math> a specific tangent vector <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V(w)\in T_{w}\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V(w)\in T_{w}\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math>. The space of smooth vector fields, denoted by <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}^{\infty}(\mathcal{M},T\mathcal{M})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}^{\infty}(\mathcal{M},T\mathcal{M})</annotation></semantics></math>, consists of all such fields <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math> where the assignment varies smoothly with <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math>. In the global coordinate system of <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}\cong\mathbb{R}^{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>≅</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}\cong\mathbb{R}^{p}</annotation></semantics></math>, any vector field <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V\in\mathcal{C}^{\infty}(\mathcal{M},T\mathcal{M})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V\in\mathcal{C}^{\infty}(\mathcal{M},T\mathcal{M})</annotation></semantics></math> can be uniquely expressed as a linear combination of the coordinate basis vectors <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\frac{\partial}{\partial w_{1}},\dots,\frac{\partial}{\partial w_{p}}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\frac{\partial}{\partial w_{1}},\dots,\frac{\partial}{\partial w_{p}}\}</annotation></semantics></math> (which form the standard basis for each <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{w}\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{w}\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math>):</p>
<table id="A6.E39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V(w)=\sum_{i=1}^{p}v_{i}(w)\frac{\partial}{\partial w_{i}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>p</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V(w)=\sum_{i=1}^{p}v_{i}(w)\frac{\partial}{\partial w_{i}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(39)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where each component function <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{i}:\mathcal{M}\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{i}:\mathcal{M}\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> is a smooth scalar function. For a function <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(Vf)|_{w}:=V(w)f(w)=\sum_{i=1}^{p}v_{i}(w)\frac{\partial}{\partial w_{i}}f(w)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>p</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Vf)|_{w}:=V(w)f(w)=\sum_{i=1}^{p}v_{i}(w)\frac{\partial}{\partial w_{i}}f(w)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="VUf:=V(Uf)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">VUf:=V(Uf)</annotation></semantics></math> for vector field <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.2 </span>The Levi-Civita Connection</h3>

<div id="A6.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In Euclidean spaces, comparing vectors at different points is trivial because the tangent spaces are identical. On a curved manifold, tangent spaces <math id="A6.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{x}\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{x}\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{y}\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{y}\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math> are distinct inner-product spaces. To differentiate vector fields, we require an affine connection <math id="A6.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∇</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla</annotation></semantics></math>, which provides a rule for connecting adjacent tangent spaces.</p>
</div>
<section id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Definition.</h4>

<div id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The Levi-Civita connection <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{(\cdot)}(\cdot):\mathcal{C}^{\infty}(\mathcal{M},T\mathcal{M})\times\mathcal{C}^{\infty}(\mathcal{M},T\mathcal{M})\to\mathcal{C}^{\infty}(\mathcal{M},T\mathcal{M})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{(\cdot)}(\cdot):\mathcal{C}^{\infty}(\mathcal{M},T\mathcal{M})\times\mathcal{C}^{\infty}(\mathcal{M},T\mathcal{M})\to\mathcal{C}^{\infty}(\mathcal{M},T\mathcal{M})</annotation></semantics></math> is the fundamental connection associated with the metric <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math>. It is uniquely determined by two geometric conditions:</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="A6.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A6.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A6.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Torsion-Free: For any vector fields <math id="A6.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X,Y\in\mathcal{C}^{\infty}(\mathcal{M},T\mathcal{M})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X,Y\in\mathcal{C}^{\infty}(\mathcal{M},T\mathcal{M})</annotation></semantics></math>, the connection is symmetric: <math id="A6.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{X}Y-\nabla_{Y}X=[X,Y]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>X</mi></msub><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>Y</mi></msub><mi>X</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{X}Y-\nabla_{Y}X=[X,Y]</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A6.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[X,Y]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[X,Y]</annotation></semantics></math> is the Lie bracket (in <math id="A6.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{p}</annotation></semantics></math>, defined by <math id="A6.I1.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[X,Y]=XY-YX" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[X,Y]=XY-YX</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A6.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Metric Compatibility: The connection preserves the inner product structure. Formally, for vector fields <math id="A6.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X,Y,Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X,Y,Z</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A6.E40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\langle Y,Z\rangle_{F}=\langle\nabla_{X}Y,Z\rangle_{F}+\langle Y,\nabla_{X}Z\rangle_{F}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>X</mi></msub><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>X</mi></msub><mi>Z</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\langle Y,Z\rangle_{F}=\langle\nabla_{X}Y,Z\rangle_{F}+\langle Y,\nabla_{X}Z\rangle_{F}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(40)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Coordinate Representation (Christoffel Symbols).</h4>

<div id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Since our manifold is globally <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{p}</annotation></semantics></math>, we can express the covariant derivative explicitly using the standard basis <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{e_{1},\dots,e_{p}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{e_{1},\dots,e_{p}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma^{k}_{ij}(w)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma^{k}_{ij}(w)</annotation></semantics></math> denote the Christoffel symbols of the second kind. The covariant derivative of a vector field <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> along <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> is given component-wise by:</p>
<table id="A6.E41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\nabla_{u}v)_{k}=\sum_{i=1}^{p}u_{i}\frac{\partial v_{k}}{\partial w_{i}}+\sum_{i,j\leq p}\Gamma^{k}_{ij}(w)u_{i}v_{j}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>u</mi></msub><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>p</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\nabla_{u}v)_{k}=\sum_{i=1}^{p}u_{i}\frac{\partial v_{k}}{\partial w_{i}}+\sum_{i,j\leq p}\Gamma^{k}_{ij}(w)u_{i}v_{j}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(41)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The first term captures the standard Euclidean directional derivative, while the second term corrects for the twisting of the coordinate system induced by the metric. The Christoffel symbols are derived from the metric <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(w)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(w)</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A6.E42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma^{k}_{ij}=\frac{1}{2}\sum_{l}(F^{-1})_{kl}\left(\frac{\partial F_{jl}}{\partial w_{i}}+\frac{\partial F_{il}}{\partial w_{j}}-\frac{\partial F_{ij}}{\partial w_{l}}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>l</mi></munder><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma^{k}_{ij}=\frac{1}{2}\sum_{l}(F^{-1})_{kl}\left(\frac{\partial F_{jl}}{\partial w_{i}}+\frac{\partial F_{il}}{\partial w_{j}}-\frac{\partial F_{ij}}{\partial w_{l}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(42)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Here, <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(F^{-1})_{kl}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(F^{-1})_{kl}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(k,l)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(k,l)</annotation></semantics></math>-entry of the inverse metric matrix, and indices denote partial derivatives with respect to coordinates. The Levi-connection would reduce to the Euclidean directional derivative when <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F=I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F=I</annotation></semantics></math>, as <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma_{ij}^{k}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma_{ij}^{k}=0</annotation></semantics></math> in this case.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.3 </span>Riemannian Gradient and Hessian</h3>

<div id="A6.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">With the metric and connection defined, we can rigorously define the following differential operators.</p>
</div>
<section id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Riemannian Gradient.</h4>

<div id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The Riemannian gradient <math id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{grad}f(w)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>grad</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{grad}f(w)</annotation></semantics></math> is the unique tangent vector representing the differential <math id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="df(w)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">df(w)</annotation></semantics></math> via the metric:</p>
<table id="A6.E43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle\text{grad}f(w),u\rangle_{F(w)}=df(w)[u]:=\lim_{\epsilon\to 0}\frac{f(w+\epsilon u)-f(w)}{\epsilon}\text{ for any }u\in\mathbb{R}^{p}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>grad</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">:=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> for any </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle\text{grad}f(w),u\rangle_{F(w)}=df(w)[u]:=\lim_{\epsilon\to 0}\frac{f(w+\epsilon u)-f(w)}{\epsilon}\text{ for any }u\in\mathbb{R}^{p}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(43)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">It has the closed form</p>
<table id="A6.E44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E44.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\text{grad}f(w)=F(w)^{-1}\nabla f(w)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>grad</mtext><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>F</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{grad}f(w)=F(w)^{-1}\nabla f(w),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(44)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla f(w)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla f(w)</annotation></semantics></math> is the standard Euclidean gradient. This confirms that the preconditioner <math id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> acts as the “inverse metric” mapping cotangent vectors (gradients) to tangent vectors (directions).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Riemannian Hessian.</h4>

<div id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The Riemannian Hessian is a linear operator on the tangent space, defined as the covariant derivative of the gradient vector field:</p>
<table id="A6.E45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Hess}f(w)[u]=\nabla_{u}\text{grad}f(w),\quad\forall u\in T_{w}\mathcal{M}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>Hess</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>u</mi></msub><mtext>grad</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Hess}f(w)[u]=\nabla_{u}\text{grad}f(w),\quad\forall u\in T_{w}\mathcal{M}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(45)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Unlike the Euclidean Hessian <math id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla^{2}f(w)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla^{2}f(w)</annotation></semantics></math>, the Riemannian Hessian accounts for the curvature of the manifold. Explicitly:</p>
<table id="A6.E46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Hess}f(w)=F(w)^{-1}\left(\nabla^{2}f(w)-\mathcal{K}(w)\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>Hess</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Hess}f(w)=F(w)^{-1}\left(\nabla^{2}f(w)-\mathcal{K}(w)\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(46)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where</p>
<table id="A6.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[\mathcal{K}(w)]_{ij}=\sum_{k=1}^{p}\Gamma^{k}_{ij}(w)\frac{\partial f}{\partial w_{k}}(w)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>p</mi></munderover><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\mathcal{K}(w)]_{ij}=\sum_{k=1}^{p}\Gamma^{k}_{ij}(w)\frac{\partial f}{\partial w_{k}}(w).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">When <math id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(w)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(w)</annotation></semantics></math> changes slowly with <math id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma_{ij}^{k}\approx 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>≈</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma_{ij}^{k}\approx 0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Hess}f(w)\approx F(w)^{-1}\nabla^{2}f(w)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>Hess</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Hess}f(w)\approx F(w)^{-1}\nabla^{2}f(w)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A7" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix G </span>Transforming the Second Order RISHD (the Riemannian ODE Framework) into a First Order System</h2>

<div id="A7.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma G.1</span></span><span id="A7.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A7.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A7.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}=\mathbb{R}^{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}=\mathbb{R}^{p}</annotation></semantics></math> be endowed with a Riemannian metric tensor <math id="A7.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(w)\succ 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≻</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(w)\succ 0</annotation></semantics></math>. For any vector fields <math id="A7.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u,v\in\mathcal{C}^{\infty}(\mathcal{M},T\mathcal{M})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u,v\in\mathcal{C}^{\infty}(\mathcal{M},T\mathcal{M})</annotation></semantics></math>, we have the following expression for the Levi-Civita connection:</span></p>
<table id="A7.E47" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.E47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{u}v=\underbrace{\partial_{u}v}_{\begin{subarray}{c}\text{Euclidean}\\
\text{derivative}\end{subarray}}+\underbrace{\frac{1}{2}F^{-1}\left[(\partial_{u}F)v+(\partial_{v}F)u-\nabla_{w}(u^{\top}Fv)\right]}_{\text{Geometric correction}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>u</mi></msub><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>u</mi></msub><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">Euclidean</mtext></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">derivative</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mi>u</mi></msub><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mi>v</mi></msub><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>w</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">Geometric correction</mtext></munder></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{u}v=\underbrace{\partial_{u}v}_{\begin{subarray}{c}\text{Euclidean}\\
\text{derivative}\end{subarray}}+\underbrace{\frac{1}{2}F^{-1}\left[(\partial_{u}F)v+(\partial_{v}F)u-\nabla_{w}(u^{\top}Fv)\right]}_{\text{Geometric correction}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(47)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A7.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A7.Thmtheorem1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.Thmtheorem1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">By Koszul formula (Corollary 5.11 in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lee, 2018</a>)</cite>), we have</span></p>
<table id="A7.E48" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A7.E48X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E48X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 2\left\langle\nabla_{u}v,h\right\rangle_{F}=\partial_{u}\left\langle v,h\right\rangle_{F}+\partial_{v}\left\langle u,h\right\rangle_{F}-\partial_{h}\left\langle u,v\right\rangle_{F}+\left\langle[u,v],h\right\rangle_{F}-\left\langle[u,h],v\right\rangle_{F}-\left\langle[v,h],u\right\rangle_{F}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>u</mi></msub><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>u</mi></msub><msub><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>v</mi></msub><msub><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>h</mi></msub><msub><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 2\left\langle\nabla_{u}v,h\right\rangle_{F}=\partial_{u}\left\langle v,h\right\rangle_{F}+\partial_{v}\left\langle u,h\right\rangle_{F}-\partial_{h}\left\langle u,v\right\rangle_{F}+\left\langle[u,v],h\right\rangle_{F}-\left\langle[u,h],v\right\rangle_{F}-\left\langle[v,h],u\right\rangle_{F}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(48)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.Thmtheorem1.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem1.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">Substituting</span></p>
<table id="A7.E49" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A7.E49X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E49X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\partial_{u}(v^{\top}Fh)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>u</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\partial_{u}(v^{\top}Fh)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E49X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(\partial_{u}v)^{\top}Fh+v^{\top}(\partial_{u}F)h+v^{\top}F(\partial_{u}h)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mi>u</mi></msub><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mi>u</mi></msub><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mi>u</mi></msub><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(\partial_{u}v)^{\top}Fh+v^{\top}(\partial_{u}F)h+v^{\top}F(\partial_{u}h),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="6" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(49)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A7.E49Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E49Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\partial_{v}(u^{\top}Fh)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>v</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\partial_{v}(u^{\top}Fh)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E49Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(\partial_{v}u)^{\top}Fh+u^{\top}(\partial_{v}F)h+u^{\top}F(\partial_{v}h)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mi>v</mi></msub><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mi>v</mi></msub><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mi>v</mi></msub><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(\partial_{v}u)^{\top}Fh+u^{\top}(\partial_{v}F)h+u^{\top}F(\partial_{v}h),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A7.E49Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E49Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\partial_{h}(u^{\top}Fv)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mo>∂</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>F</mi><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\partial_{h}(u^{\top}Fv)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E49Xb.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-(\partial_{h}u)^{\top}Fv-u^{\top}(\partial_{h}F)v-u^{\top}F(\partial_{h}v)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mi>h</mi></msub><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mi>h</mi></msub><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mi>h</mi></msub><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-(\partial_{h}u)^{\top}Fv-u^{\top}(\partial_{h}F)v-u^{\top}F(\partial_{h}v),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A7.E49Xc" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E49Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle[u,v]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle[u,v]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E49Xc.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\partial_{u}v-\partial_{v}u," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>u</mi></msub><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>v</mi></msub><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\partial_{u}v-\partial_{v}u,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A7.E49Xd" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E49Xd.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle[u,h]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle[u,h]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E49Xd.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\partial_{u}h-\partial_{h}u," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>u</mi></msub><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>h</mi></msub><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\partial_{u}h-\partial_{h}u,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A7.E49Xe" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E49Xe.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle[v,h]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle[v,h]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E49Xe.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\partial_{v}h-\partial_{h}v," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>v</mi></msub><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>h</mi></msub><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\partial_{v}h-\partial_{h}v,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.Thmtheorem1.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem1.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">into (<a href="#A7.E48" title="Equation 48 ‣ Proof. ‣ Lemma G.1. ‣ Appendix G Transforming the Second Order RISHD (the Riemannian ODE Framework) into a First Order System ‣ Accelerating LLM Pre-Training through Flat-Direction Dynamics Enhancement" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">48</span></a>) yields</span></p>
<table id="A7.E50" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.E50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2h^{\top}F\nabla_{u}v=h^{\top}\left[2F\partial_{u}v+(\partial_{u}F)v+(\partial_{v}F)u-\nabla_{w}(u^{\top}Fv)\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>u</mi></msub><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>u</mi></msub><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mi>u</mi></msub><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mi>v</mi></msub><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>w</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2h^{\top}F\nabla_{u}v=h^{\top}\left[2F\partial_{u}v+(\partial_{u}F)v+(\partial_{v}F)u-\nabla_{w}(u^{\top}Fv)\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(50)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.Thmtheorem1.p2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem1.p2.5.1" class="ltx_text">We get the conclusion.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.Thmtheorem1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.Thmtheorem1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A7.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition G.2</span></span><span id="A7.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A7.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.Thmtheorem2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A7.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}=\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}=\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> be endowed with a Riemannian metric tensor <math id="A7.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(w)\succ 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≻</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(w)\succ 0</annotation></semantics></math>. Then the RISHD</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.E51"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla_{\dot{w}_{t}}\dot{w}_{t}+\alpha_{t}\dot{w}_{t}+\beta_{t}\nabla_{\dot{w}_{t}}\operatorname{grad}f(w_{t})+\gamma_{t}\operatorname{grad}f(w_{t})=0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>grad</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>grad</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla_{\dot{w}_{t}}\dot{w}_{t}+\alpha_{t}\dot{w}_{t}+\beta_{t}\nabla_{\dot{w}_{t}}\operatorname{grad}f(w_{t})+\gamma_{t}\operatorname{grad}f(w_{t})=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(51)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.Thmtheorem2.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem2.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">with <math id="A7.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}=\alpha-\dot{\eta}_{t}/\eta_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}=\alpha-\dot{\eta}_{t}/\eta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A7.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{t}=\beta\eta_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{t}=\beta\eta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A7.Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{t}=\eta_{t}(\alpha\beta+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{t}=\eta_{t}(\alpha\beta+1)</annotation></semantics></math> is equivalent to the following first order system:</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.E52"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{cases}\dot{w}_{t}=-\eta_{t}F(w_{t})^{-1}(m_{t}+\beta\nabla f(w_{t})),\\
\dot{m}_{t}=-\alpha m_{t}+\nabla f(w_{t})+R_{t},\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>η</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>m</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{cases}\dot{w}_{t}=-\eta_{t}F(w_{t})^{-1}(m_{t}+\beta\nabla f(w_{t})),\\
\dot{m}_{t}=-\alpha m_{t}+\nabla f(w_{t})+R_{t},\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(52)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.Thmtheorem2.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem2.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where we define <math id="A7.Thmtheorem2.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="u_{t}=m_{t}+\beta\nabla f(w_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{t}=m_{t}+\beta\nabla f(w_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> and</span></p>
<table id="A7.E53" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A7.E53X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E53X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle R_{t}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle R_{t}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E53X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\frac{\eta_{t}}{2}\nabla_{w}(u_{t}^{\top}F(w_{t})u_{t})+\frac{\beta\eta_{t}}{2}\left(\nabla F(w_{t})[F^{-1}(w_{t})u_{t}]F^{-1}(w_{t})\nabla f(w_{t})-\nabla F(w_{t})[F^{-1}(w_{t})\nabla f(w_{t})]F^{-1}(w_{t})u_{t}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>w</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>u</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>(</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>F</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>u</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mi>F</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>F</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mi>F</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>u</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\frac{\eta_{t}}{2}\nabla_{w}(u_{t}^{\top}F(w_{t})u_{t})+\frac{\beta\eta_{t}}{2}\left(\nabla F(w_{t})[F^{-1}(w_{t})u_{t}]F^{-1}(w_{t})\nabla f(w_{t})-\nabla F(w_{t})[F^{-1}(w_{t})\nabla f(w_{t})]F^{-1}(w_{t})u_{t}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(53)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A7.E53Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E53Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\frac{\beta\eta_{t}}{2}\nabla F(w_{t})[F^{-1}(w_{t})u_{t}]F^{-1}(w_{t})\nabla f(w_{t})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>F</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>u</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mi>F</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\frac{\beta\eta_{t}}{2}\nabla F(w_{t})[F^{-1}(w_{t})u_{t}]F^{-1}(w_{t})\nabla f(w_{t}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A7.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Remark G.3</span></span><span id="A7.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="A7.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">(<a href="#A7.E53" title="Equation 53 ‣ Proposition G.2. ‣ Appendix G Transforming the Second Order RISHD (the Riemannian ODE Framework) into a First Order System ‣ Accelerating LLM Pre-Training through Flat-Direction Dynamics Enhancement" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">53</span></a>) is equivalent to (<a href="#S4.E3" title="Equation 3 ‣ Continuous-time Viewpoint. ‣ 4.2 The Riemannian ODE Framework ‣ 4 A Unified Riemannian ODE Framework for Understanding Adaptive Algorithms ‣ Accelerating LLM Pre-Training through Flat-Direction Dynamics Enhancement" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>) as <math id="A7.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\dot{w}_{t}}\operatorname{grad}f(w_{t})=\operatorname{Hess}(w_{t})\dot{w}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>grad</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Hess</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\dot{w}_{t}}\operatorname{grad}f(w_{t})=\operatorname{Hess}(w_{t})\dot{w}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A7.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A7.Thmtheorem2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.Thmtheorem2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">First, we let <math id="A7.Thmtheorem2.p2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="m_{t}=-F(w_{t})\dot{w}_{t}/\eta_{t}-\beta\nabla f(w_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{t}=-F(w_{t})\dot{w}_{t}/\eta_{t}-\beta\nabla f(w_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> and get</span></p>
<table id="A7.E54" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A7.E54X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E54X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\dot{w}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\dot{w}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E54X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\eta_{t}F(w_{t})^{-1}(m_{t}+\beta\nabla f(w_{t}))," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>η</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\eta_{t}F(w_{t})^{-1}(m_{t}+\beta\nabla f(w_{t})),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(54)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A7.E54Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E54Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ddot{w}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>¨</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ddot{w}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E54Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\dot{\eta}_{t}F(w_{t})^{-1}(m_{t}+\beta\nabla f(w_{t}))-\eta_{t}\frac{d}{dt}F(w_{t})^{-1}(m_{t}+\beta\nabla f(w_{t}))-\eta_{t}F(w_{t})^{-1}(\dot{m}_{t}+\beta\nabla^{2}f(w_{t})\dot{w}_{t})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>m</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\dot{\eta}_{t}F(w_{t})^{-1}(m_{t}+\beta\nabla f(w_{t}))-\eta_{t}\frac{d}{dt}F(w_{t})^{-1}(m_{t}+\beta\nabla f(w_{t}))-\eta_{t}F(w_{t})^{-1}(\dot{m}_{t}+\beta\nabla^{2}f(w_{t})\dot{w}_{t}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.Thmtheorem2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">By Lemma <a href="#A7.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma G.1. ‣ Appendix G Transforming the Second Order RISHD (the Riemannian ODE Framework) into a First Order System ‣ Accelerating LLM Pre-Training through Flat-Direction Dynamics Enhancement" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G.1</span></a>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A7.E55" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.E55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\dot{w}_{t}}\dot{w}_{t}=\ddot{w}_{t}+F(w_{t})^{-1}\dot{F}(w_{t})\dot{w}_{t}-\frac{1}{2}F^{-1}(w_{t})\nabla_{w}(\dot{w}_{t}^{\top}F(w)\dot{w}_{t})|_{w=w_{t}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>¨</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>w</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\dot{w}_{t}}\dot{w}_{t}=\ddot{w}_{t}+F(w_{t})^{-1}\dot{F}(w_{t})\dot{w}_{t}-\frac{1}{2}F^{-1}(w_{t})\nabla_{w}(\dot{w}_{t}^{\top}F(w)\dot{w}_{t})|_{w=w_{t}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(55)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.Thmtheorem2.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem2.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">and</span></p>
<table id="A7.E56" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A7.E56X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E56X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla_{\dot{w}_{t}}\operatorname{grad}f(w_{t})=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>grad</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla_{\dot{w}_{t}}\operatorname{grad}f(w_{t})=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E56X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla_{\dot{w}_{t}}(F^{-1}(w_{t})\nabla f(w_{t}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>F</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla_{\dot{w}_{t}}(F^{-1}(w_{t})\nabla f(w_{t}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="5" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(56)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A7.E56Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E56Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E56Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{d}{dt}{(F^{-1}(w_{t}))}\nabla f(w_{t})+F^{-1}(w_{t})\nabla^{2}f(w_{t})\dot{w}_{t}+\frac{1}{2}F^{-1}(w_{t})\frac{d}{dt}F(w_{t})F^{-1}(w_{t})\nabla f(w_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>F</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>F</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mi>F</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>F</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{d}{dt}{(F^{-1}(w_{t}))}\nabla f(w_{t})+F^{-1}(w_{t})\nabla^{2}f(w_{t})\dot{w}_{t}+\frac{1}{2}F^{-1}(w_{t})\frac{d}{dt}F(w_{t})F^{-1}(w_{t})\nabla f(w_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A7.E56Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E56Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\frac{1}{2}F^{-1}(w_{t})\nabla F(w_{t})[F^{-1}(w_{t})\nabla f(w_{t})]\dot{w}_{t}-\frac{1}{2}F^{-1}(w_{t})\nabla_{w}(\dot{w}_{t}^{\top}F(w)F^{-1}(w_{t})\nabla f(w_{t})|_{w=w_{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mi>F</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>F</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mi>F</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>w</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>F</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\frac{1}{2}F^{-1}(w_{t})\nabla F(w_{t})[F^{-1}(w_{t})\nabla f(w_{t})]\dot{w}_{t}-\frac{1}{2}F^{-1}(w_{t})\nabla_{w}(\dot{w}_{t}^{\top}F(w)F^{-1}(w_{t})\nabla f(w_{t})|_{w=w_{t}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A7.E56Xc" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E56Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E56Xc.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle F^{-1}(w_{t})\nabla^{2}f(w_{t})\dot{w}_{t}-\frac{1}{2}F^{-1}(w_{t})\frac{d}{dt}F(w_{t})F^{-1}(w_{t})\nabla f(w_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mi>F</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>F</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle F^{-1}(w_{t})\nabla^{2}f(w_{t})\dot{w}_{t}-\frac{1}{2}F^{-1}(w_{t})\frac{d}{dt}F(w_{t})F^{-1}(w_{t})\nabla f(w_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A7.E56Xd" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E56Xd.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\frac{1}{2}F^{-1}(w_{t})\nabla F(w_{t})[F^{-1}(w_{t})\nabla f(w_{t})]\dot{w}_{t}-\frac{1}{2}F^{-1}(w_{t})\nabla_{w}(\dot{w}_{t}^{\top}F(w)F^{-1}(w_{t})\nabla f(w_{t})|_{w=w_{t}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mi>F</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>F</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mi>F</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>w</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>F</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\frac{1}{2}F^{-1}(w_{t})\nabla F(w_{t})[F^{-1}(w_{t})\nabla f(w_{t})]\dot{w}_{t}-\frac{1}{2}F^{-1}(w_{t})\nabla_{w}(\dot{w}_{t}^{\top}F(w)F^{-1}(w_{t})\nabla f(w_{t})|_{w=w_{t}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A7.Thmtheorem2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.Thmtheorem2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Substituting them into (<a href="#A7.E51" title="Equation 51 ‣ Proposition G.2. ‣ Appendix G Transforming the Second Order RISHD (the Riemannian ODE Framework) into a First Order System ‣ Accelerating LLM Pre-Training through Flat-Direction Dynamics Enhancement" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">51</span></a>) yields</span></p>
<table id="A7.E57" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A7.E57X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E57X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\dot{m}_{t}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>m</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\dot{m}_{t}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E57X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\alpha m_{t}+\nabla f(w_{t})-\frac{\eta_{t}}{2}\nabla_{w}(u_{t}^{\top}F(w_{t})u_{t})-\frac{\beta}{2}\nabla F(w_{t})[\dot{w}_{t}]F^{-1}(w_{t})\nabla f(w_{t})+\frac{\beta}{2}\nabla F(w_{t})[F^{-1}(w_{t})\nabla f(w_{t})]\dot{w}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><mi>m</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>w</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>u</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mi>F</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>F</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\alpha m_{t}+\nabla f(w_{t})-\frac{\eta_{t}}{2}\nabla_{w}(u_{t}^{\top}F(w_{t})u_{t})-\frac{\beta}{2}\nabla F(w_{t})[\dot{w}_{t}]F^{-1}(w_{t})\nabla f(w_{t})+\frac{\beta}{2}\nabla F(w_{t})[F^{-1}(w_{t})\nabla f(w_{t})]\dot{w}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(57)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A7.E57Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E57Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\frac{\beta}{2}\nabla F(w_{t})[\dot{w}_{t}]F^{-1}(w_{t})\nabla f(w_{t})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mi>F</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\frac{\beta}{2}\nabla F(w_{t})[\dot{w}_{t}]F^{-1}(w_{t})\nabla f(w_{t}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.Thmtheorem2.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">We get the conclusion.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A7.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Remark G.4</span></span><span id="A7.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="A7.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In general, we assume that <math id="A7.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(w)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(w)</annotation></semantics></math> varies slowly with respect to <math id="A7.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> to ensure the stability of the preconditioner. This assumption is practically justified by the common use of Exponential Moving Average (EMA) with a decay coefficient close to <math id="A7.Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>, which enforces a smooth evolution of the estimated preconditioner. Consequently, based on the expression of <math id="A7.Thmtheorem4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#A7.E53" title="Equation 53 ‣ Proposition G.2. ‣ Appendix G Transforming the Second Order RISHD (the Riemannian ODE Framework) into a First Order System ‣ Accelerating LLM Pre-Training through Flat-Direction Dynamics Enhancement" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">53</span></a>), this term is typically negligible relative to <math id="A7.Thmtheorem4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.Thmtheorem4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla f(w_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla f(w_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>, as it scales with the small step size <math id="A7.Thmtheorem4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and the limited variation <math id="A7.Thmtheorem4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\nabla F(w)\|_{\mathrm{op}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\nabla F(w)\|_{\mathrm{op}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix H </span>Theoretical Analysis on Quadratic Objectives: An Illustrative Example</h2>

<div id="A8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To elucidate the acceleration mechanism of <span id="A8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">LITE</span>, we analyze the discrete-time dynamics of the update rule (<a href="#S4.E2" title="Equation 2 ‣ 4.1 A Unified Discrete Formulation ‣ 4 A Unified Riemannian ODE Framework for Understanding Adaptive Algorithms ‣ Accelerating LLM Pre-Training through Flat-Direction Dynamics Enhancement" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>), which corresponds to non-accelerated adaptive optimizers, on a quadratic objective function:</p>
<table id="A8.E58" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.E58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(w)=\frac{1}{2}\sum_{i=1}^{p}\lambda_{i}w_{i}^{2}+b^{\top}w." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>p</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(w)=\frac{1}{2}\sum_{i=1}^{p}\lambda_{i}w_{i}^{2}+b^{\top}w.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(58)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We assume the eigenvalues are sorted as <math id="A8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{1}&gt;\dots&gt;\lambda_{k}&gt;0\geq\dots\geq\lambda_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">⋯</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>≥</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">⋯</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{1}&gt;\dots&gt;\lambda_{k}&gt;0\geq\dots\geq\lambda_{p}</annotation></semantics></math>, representing an anisotropic landscape where negative <math id="A8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> correspond to local nonconvex directions. For simplicity, we set the step size <math id="A8.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h=1</annotation></semantics></math> and the preconditioner <math id="A8.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(w)=I_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(w)=I_{p}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since the Hessian is diagonal, the dynamics decouple across coordinates.</p>
</div>
<div id="A8.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A8.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{\star}=-[b_{1}/\lambda_{1},\dots,b_{p}/\lambda_{p}]^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{\star}=-[b_{1}/\lambda_{1},\dots,b_{p}/\lambda_{p}]^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the stationary point. To characterize the trajectory of the error term <math id="A8.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{k}=w_{k}-w_{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{k}=w_{k}-w_{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>, we eliminate the auxiliary momentum variable <math id="A8.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>.
From (<a href="#S4.E2" title="Equation 2 ‣ 4.1 A Unified Discrete Formulation ‣ 4 A Unified Riemannian ODE Framework for Understanding Adaptive Algorithms ‣ Accelerating LLM Pre-Training through Flat-Direction Dynamics Enhancement" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>) with <math id="A8.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F=I_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F=I_{p}</annotation></semantics></math>, the <math id="A8.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th coordinate of <math id="A8.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> can be expressed in terms of <math id="A8.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> as:</p>
<table id="A8.E59" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.E59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta(m_{k})_{i}=(1-\eta\beta\lambda_{i})(e_{k})_{i}-(e_{k+1})_{i},\quad 1\leq i\leq p." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta(m_{k})_{i}=(1-\eta\beta\lambda_{i})(e_{k})_{i}-(e_{k+1})_{i},\quad 1\leq i\leq p.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(59)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Applying a time shift to (<a href="#A8.E59" title="Equation 59 ‣ Appendix H Theoretical Analysis on Quadratic Objectives: An Illustrative Example ‣ Accelerating LLM Pre-Training through Flat-Direction Dynamics Enhancement" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">59</span></a>), we obtain:</p>
<table id="A8.E60" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.E60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta(m_{k-1})_{i}=(1-\eta\beta\lambda_{i})(e_{k-1})_{i}-(e_{k})_{i}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta(m_{k-1})_{i}=(1-\eta\beta\lambda_{i})(e_{k-1})_{i}-(e_{k})_{i}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(60)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.p2.3" class="ltx_p">Combining these relations leads to a homogeneous second-order linear recurrence:</p>
<table id="A8.E61" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.E61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(e_{k+1})_{i}-2T_{i}(e_{k})_{i}+D_{i}(e_{k-1})_{i}=0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(e_{k+1})_{i}-2T_{i}(e_{k})_{i}+D_{i}(e_{k-1})_{i}=0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(61)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.p2.4" class="ltx_p">where the coefficients are defined as:</p>
<table id="A8.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A8.E62"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.E62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle T_{i}=T(\lambda_{i}):=1-\frac{\alpha+\eta\lambda_{i}(\beta+1)}{2},\quad D_{i}=D(\lambda_{i}):=(1-\alpha)(1-\eta\beta\lambda_{i})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle T_{i}=T(\lambda_{i}):=1-\frac{\alpha+\eta\lambda_{i}(\beta+1)}{2},\quad D_{i}=D(\lambda_{i}):=(1-\alpha)(1-\eta\beta\lambda_{i}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(62)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.p2.5" class="ltx_p">The characteristic equation is given by <math id="A8.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{2}-2T_{i}r+D_{i}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{2}-2T_{i}r+D_{i}=0</annotation></semantics></math>, with roots:</p>
<table id="A8.E63" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.E63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i,1,2}=T_{i}\pm\sqrt{T_{i}^{2}-D_{i}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>±</mo><msqrt><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i,1,2}=T_{i}\pm\sqrt{T_{i}^{2}-D_{i}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(63)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.p2.6" class="ltx_p">Based on the discriminant <math id="A8.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{i}=T_{i}^{2}-D_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{i}=T_{i}^{2}-D_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, the dynamics fall into three regimes, yielding the following closed-form solutions (<math id="A8.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{i,1},c_{i,2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{i,1},c_{i,2}</annotation></semantics></math> are constants determined by initialization):</p>
<table id="A8.EGx20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A8.E64"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.E64.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle w_{k,i}=-\dfrac{b_{i}}{\lambda_{i}}+\begin{cases}c_{i,1}r_{i,1}^{k}+c_{i,2}r_{i,2}^{k},&amp;\Delta_{i}&gt;0\ \text{({Overdamped})},\\
(c_{i,1}+c_{i,2}k)D_{i}^{k/2},&amp;\Delta_{i}=0\ \text{({Critically damped})},\\
D_{i}^{k/2}\left[c_{i,1}\cos(k\theta_{i})+c_{i,2}\sin(k\theta_{i})\right],&amp;\Delta_{i}&lt;0\ \text{({Underdamped})},\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mtext>(</mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">Overdamped</mtext><mtext>)</mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mtext>(</mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">Critically damped</mtext><mtext>)</mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mtext>(</mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">Underdamped</mtext><mtext>)</mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle w_{k,i}=-\dfrac{b_{i}}{\lambda_{i}}+\begin{cases}c_{i,1}r_{i,1}^{k}+c_{i,2}r_{i,2}^{k},&amp;\Delta_{i}&gt;0\ \text{({Overdamped})},\\
(c_{i,1}+c_{i,2}k)D_{i}^{k/2},&amp;\Delta_{i}=0\ \text{({Critically damped})},\\
D_{i}^{k/2}\left[c_{i,1}\cos(k\theta_{i})+c_{i,2}\sin(k\theta_{i})\right],&amp;\Delta_{i}&lt;0\ \text{({Underdamped})},\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(64)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.p2.7" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A8.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{i}=\arccos(T_{i}/\sqrt{D_{i}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>arccos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msqrt></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{i}=\arccos(T_{i}/\sqrt{D_{i}})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Stability Analysis.</h4>

<div id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Convergence in convex directions requires the magnitude of all characteristic roots to be at most <math id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>. According to the Jury Stability Criterion, the necessary and sufficient conditions are <math id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|P_{i}(0)|\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|P_{i}(0)|\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}(1)\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}(1)\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}(-1)\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}(-1)\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}(z)=z^{2}-2T_{i}z+D_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}(z)=z^{2}-2T_{i}z+D_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. Solving these inequalities yields the stability bound:</p>
<table id="A8.E65" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.E65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta\leq\frac{2(2-\alpha)}{\lambda_{1}\max\{1+2\beta-\alpha\beta,\,2\beta(1-\alpha)\}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn> 2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta\leq\frac{2(2-\alpha)}{\lambda_{1}\max\{1+2\beta-\alpha\beta,\,2\beta(1-\alpha)\}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(65)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Ideally, this condition confirms that the maximum allowable step size is governed by the sharpest direction <math id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Regime Classification.</h4>

<div id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We next analyze how the curvature <math id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> determines the dynamic regime. The equation <math id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T(\lambda)^{2}=D(\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T(\lambda)^{2}=D(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to <math id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A8.E66" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.E66.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(1-\frac{\alpha+\eta\lambda(\beta+1)}{2}\right)^{2}=(1-\alpha)(1-\eta\beta\lambda)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(1-\frac{\alpha+\eta\lambda(\beta+1)}{2}\right)^{2}=(1-\alpha)(1-\eta\beta\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(66)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">possesses two real positive roots, denoted <math id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\lambda}_{1}&lt;\tilde{\lambda}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\lambda}_{1}&lt;\tilde{\lambda}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. By the properties of quadratic functions, we refer eigenvalues <math id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying <math id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda&lt;\tilde{\lambda}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda&lt;\tilde{\lambda}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> to <em id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">flat directions (parts)</em>, which fall into the <span id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">overdamped regime</span>. Conversely, eigenvalues <math id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\geq\tilde{\lambda}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\geq\tilde{\lambda}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> correspond to <em id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.2.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">sharp directions</em>, whose dynamic regimes depend on the specific magnitude of the curvature (typically transitioning into the underdamped regime).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Acceleration Mechanism of <span id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">LITE</span>.</h4>

<div id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Here we suppose that the stability condition (<a href="#A8.E65" title="Equation 65 ‣ Stability Analysis. ‣ Appendix H Theoretical Analysis on Quadratic Objectives: An Illustrative Example ‣ Accelerating LLM Pre-Training through Flat-Direction Dynamics Enhancement" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">65</span></a>) holds. Since <span id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">LITE</span> explicitly increases <math id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> in flat directions, we focus our analysis on the regime <math id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{i}&lt;\tilde{\lambda}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{i}&lt;\tilde{\lambda}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. In this regime, the dynamics are overdamped, and dominated by the larger root <math id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{1}=T+\sqrt{T^{2}-D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{1}=T+\sqrt{T^{2}-D}</annotation></semantics></math>. We demonstrate that our parameter adjustment modifies <math id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> to facilitate escape from nonconvex regions and foster convergence in convex regions.</p>
</div>
<div id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We analyze the sensitivity of <math id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> case by case:</p>
</div>
<div id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="A8.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A8.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A8.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Case 1: Flat Nonconvex Directions (<math id="A8.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>).</span>
The coefficients become <math id="A8.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=1-\frac{\alpha}{2}+\frac{\eta|\lambda|(\beta+1)}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=1-\frac{\alpha}{2}+\frac{\eta|\lambda|(\beta+1)}{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A8.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D=(1-\alpha)(1+\eta\beta|\lambda|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D=(1-\alpha)(1+\eta\beta|\lambda|)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Clearly, <math id="A8.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T&gt;1-\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T&gt;1-\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>, and both <math id="A8.I1.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A8.I1.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> are strictly increasing functions of <math id="A8.I1.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A8.I1.i1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math>.
Consider the partial derivatives:</p>
<table id="A8.E67" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.E67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial r_{1}}{\partial\beta}=\frac{\partial T}{\partial\beta}+\frac{1}{2\sqrt{T^{2}-D}}\left(2T\frac{\partial T}{\partial\beta}-\frac{\partial D}{\partial\beta}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial r_{1}}{\partial\beta}=\frac{\partial T}{\partial\beta}+\frac{1}{2\sqrt{T^{2}-D}}\left(2T\frac{\partial T}{\partial\beta}-\frac{\partial D}{\partial\beta}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(67)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.I1.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A8.I1.i1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, and noting that:</p>
<table id="A8.E68" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.E68.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2T\frac{\partial T}{\partial\beta}-\frac{\partial D}{\partial\beta}=T\eta|\lambda|-(1-\alpha)\eta|\lambda|&gt;0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2T\frac{\partial T}{\partial\beta}-\frac{\partial D}{\partial\beta}=T\eta|\lambda|-(1-\alpha)\eta|\lambda|&gt;0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(68)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.I1.i1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">(and similarly for <math id="A8.I1.i1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math>), we conclude that increasing <math id="A8.I1.i1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A8.I1.i1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> yields a strictly larger <math id="A8.I1.i1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> (with <math id="A8.I1.i1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{1}&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{1}&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>). This increases the exponential divergence rate along negative curvature directions, thereby facilitating rapid escape.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A8.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A8.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Case 2: Flat Convex Directions (<math id="A8.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\lambda&lt;\tilde{\lambda}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\lambda&lt;\tilde{\lambda}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>).</span>
In this regime, the convergence rate is governed by how quickly <math id="A8.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> decays to zero. To accelerate convergence, we must <span id="A8.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">minimize</span> <math id="A8.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The coefficients are <math id="A8.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=1-\frac{\alpha+\eta\lambda(\beta+1)}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=1-\frac{\alpha+\eta\lambda(\beta+1)}{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A8.I1.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D=(1-\alpha)(1-\eta\beta\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D=(1-\alpha)(1-\eta\beta\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Observing the monotonicity:</p>
<table id="A8.E69" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.E69.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\frac{\partial T}{\partial\beta}&lt;0,\quad\frac{\partial D}{\partial\beta}&lt;0\quad(\text{and similarly for }\eta)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>and similarly for </mtext><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial T}{\partial\beta}&lt;0,\quad\frac{\partial D}{\partial\beta}&lt;0\quad(\text{and similarly for }\eta).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(69)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.I1.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Both <math id="A8.I1.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A8.I1.i2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> decrease monotonically as <math id="A8.I1.i2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A8.I1.i2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> increases. Since <math id="A8.I1.i2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is strictly increasing with respect to <math id="A8.I1.i2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A8.I1.i2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>, the dominant root <math id="A8.I1.i2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> decreases when <math id="A8.I1.i2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> (or <math id="A8.I1.i2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math>) increases. This reduction in the spectral radius directly fosters faster convergence.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A9" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix I </span>Some Common Adaptive Optimizers for LLM Pre-training</h2>

<div id="A9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A9.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Here we list some common optimizers in LLM pre-training. They can be subsumed by discretizing the ODE framework (<a href="#S4.E2" title="Equation 2 ‣ 4.1 A Unified Discrete Formulation ‣ 4 A Unified Riemannian ODE Framework for Understanding Adaptive Algorithms ‣ Accelerating LLM Pre-Training through Flat-Direction Dynamics Enhancement" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>). We omit gradient clipping and AdamW-type bias correction coefficient <math id="A9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1-\theta^{t}}{\sqrt{1-\beta_{v}^{t}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow></msqrt></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1-\theta^{t}}{\sqrt{1-\beta_{v}^{t}}}</annotation></semantics></math> for notational brevity.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg2" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 2</span> </span> AdamW</figcaption>
<div id="alg2.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg2.l0" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l0.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">0:</span></span>
            
            
           Hyper-parameters: <math id="alg2.l0.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg2.l0.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{v}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg2.l0.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg2.l0.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\eta_{t}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\eta_{t}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg2.l0.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
           Initialize <math id="alg2.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg2.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v=0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg2.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=0</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
           <span id="alg2.l2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg2.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1,2,\dots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1,2,\dots</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg2.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
            Compute stochastic gradient <math id="alg2.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> at current parameters <math id="alg2.l3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg2.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
            <math id="alg2.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{t}=\theta m_{t-1}+(1-\theta)g_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{t}=\theta m_{t-1}+(1-\theta)g_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
            <math id="alg2.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{t}=\beta_{v}v_{t-1}+(1-\beta_{v})g_{t}^{\odot 2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{t}=\beta_{v}v_{t-1}+(1-\beta_{v})g_{t}^{\odot 2}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
            <math id="alg2.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{t+1}=w_{t}-\eta_{t}\left(\frac{{m}_{t}}{\sqrt{{v}_{t}}+\epsilon}+\lambda w_{t}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{t+1}=w_{t}-\eta_{t}\left(\frac{{m}_{t}}{\sqrt{{v}_{t}}+\epsilon}+\lambda w_{t}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
           <span id="alg2.l7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg2.l7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
</div>
</figure>
<figure id="alg3" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 3</span> </span> Lion</figcaption>
<div id="alg3.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg3.l0" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l0.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">0:</span></span>
            
            
           <math id="alg3.l0.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta,\beta_{v},\{\eta_{t}\},\epsilon,\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta,\beta_{v},\{\eta_{t}\},\epsilon,\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
           Initialize <math id="alg3.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=0</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
           <span id="alg3.l2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg3.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1,2,\dots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1,2,\dots</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg3.l2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg3.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
            Compute gradient <math id="alg3.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> at current parameters <math id="alg3.l3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
            <math id="alg3.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{t}=\theta m_{t-1}+(1-\theta)g_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{t}=\theta m_{t-1}+(1-\theta)g_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
            <math id="alg3.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{t}=\beta_{v}m_{t-1}+(1-\beta_{v})g_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{t}=\beta_{v}m_{t-1}+(1-\beta_{v})g_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
            <math id="alg3.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{t+1}=w_{t}-\eta_{t}\operatorname{sign}(u_{t})-\eta_{t}\lambda w_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>sign</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{t+1}=w_{t}-\eta_{t}\operatorname{sign}(u_{t})-\eta_{t}\lambda w_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
           <span id="alg3.l7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg3.l7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
</div>
</figure>
<figure id="alg4" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 4</span> </span> MARS</figcaption>
<div id="alg4.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg4.l0" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg4.l0.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">0:</span></span>
            
            
           <math id="alg4.l0.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta,\beta_{v},\gamma,\epsilon,\{\eta_{t}\},\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta,\beta_{v},\gamma,\epsilon,\{\eta_{t}\},\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg4.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
           Initialize <math id="alg4.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg4.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v=0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg4.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{0}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{0}=0</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg4.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
           <span id="alg4.l2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg4.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1,2,\dots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1,2,\dots</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg4.l2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg4.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
            Compute stochastic gradient <math id="alg4.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> at current parameters <math id="alg4.l3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg4.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
            <math id="alg4.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle c_{t}=g_{t}+\gamma\frac{\theta}{1-\theta}(g_{t}-g_{t-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle c_{t}=g_{t}+\gamma\frac{\theta}{1-\theta}(g_{t}-g_{t-1})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg4.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
            <math id="alg4.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{t}=\theta m_{t-1}+(1-\theta){c}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{t}=\theta m_{t-1}+(1-\theta){c}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg4.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
            <math id="alg4.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{t}=\beta_{v}v_{t-1}+(1-\beta_{v}){c}_{t}^{\odot 2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{t}=\beta_{v}v_{t-1}+(1-\beta_{v}){c}_{t}^{\odot 2}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg4.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
            <math id="alg4.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle w_{t+1}=w_{t}-\eta_{t}\frac{{m}_{t}}{\sqrt{{v}_{t}}+\epsilon}-\eta_{t}\lambda w_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle w_{t+1}=w_{t}-\eta_{t}\frac{{m}_{t}}{\sqrt{{v}_{t}}+\epsilon}-\eta_{t}\lambda w_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg4.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
           <span id="alg4.l8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg4.l8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
</div>
</figure>
<div id="A9.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A9.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Remark I.1</span></span><span id="A9.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="A9.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A9.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In MARS, the momentum term is updated as:</p>
<table id="A9.E70" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A9.E70.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{t}=\theta m_{t-1}+(1-\theta)g_{t}+\gamma\theta(g_{t}-g_{t-1})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{t}=\theta m_{t-1}+(1-\theta)g_{t}+\gamma\theta(g_{t}-g_{t-1}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(70)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">It can be transformer to the formulation in (<a href="#S4.E2" title="Equation 2 ‣ 4.1 A Unified Discrete Formulation ‣ 4 A Unified Riemannian ODE Framework for Understanding Adaptive Algorithms ‣ Accelerating LLM Pre-Training through Flat-Direction Dynamics Enhancement" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>) as:</p>
<table id="A9.E71" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A9.E71X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E71X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle s_{t}=\theta s_{t-1}+g_{t},\quad\tilde{m}_{t}=s_{t}+\frac{\gamma}{(1-\gamma)(1-\theta)}g_{t}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>θ</mi><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>g</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>m</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>g</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle s_{t}=\theta s_{t-1}+g_{t},\quad\tilde{m}_{t}=s_{t}+\frac{\gamma}{(1-\gamma)(1-\theta)}g_{t},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(71)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.Thmtheorem1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">with <math id="A9.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{t}=(1-\gamma)(1-\theta)\tilde{m}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>m</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{t}=(1-\gamma)(1-\theta)\tilde{m}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. Note that <math id="A9.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\neq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\neq 1</annotation></semantics></math>; otherwise, (<a href="#A9.E70" title="Equation 70 ‣ Remark I.1. ‣ Appendix I Some Common Adaptive Optimizers for LLM Pre-training ‣ Accelerating LLM Pre-Training through Flat-Direction Dynamics Enhancement" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">70</span></a>) would reduce to
<math id="A9.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{t}=\theta m_{t-1}-\theta g_{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{t}=\theta m_{t-1}-\theta g_{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, thereby completely discarding the current gradient information <math id="A9.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<figure id="alg5" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 5</span> </span> Muon</figcaption>
<div id="alg5.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg5.l0" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg5.l0.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">0:</span></span>
            
            
           <math id="alg5.l0.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{\operatorname{muon}},\eta,\epsilon,\theta_{\operatorname{adamw}},\beta_{v},\{\eta_{t}\},\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>muon</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>adamw</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{\operatorname{muon}},\eta,\epsilon,\theta_{\operatorname{adamw}},\beta_{v},\{\eta_{t}\},\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg5.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
           Initialize state <math id="alg5.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg5.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
           <span id="alg5.l2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg5.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1,2,\dots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1,2,\dots</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg5.l2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg5.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
            <span id="alg5.l3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">For weights in Output, Embedding, and Norm layers:</span>

</div>
<div id="alg5.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
             Update using AdamW with hyper-parameters <math id="alg5.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{\operatorname{adamw}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>adamw</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{\operatorname{adamw}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg5.l4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{v}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg5.l4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg5.l4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg5.l4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg5.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
            <span id="alg5.l5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">For weight matrices in transformer layers:</span>

</div>
<div id="alg5.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
             Compute stochastic gradient <math id="alg5.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> at current parameters <math id="alg5.l6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg5.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
             <math id="alg5.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{t}=\theta_{\operatorname{muon}}m_{t-1}+g_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>muon</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{t}=\theta_{\operatorname{muon}}m_{t-1}+g_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg5.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
             <math id="alg5.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{t}=\theta_{\operatorname{muon}}m_{t}+g_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>muon</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{t}=\theta_{\operatorname{muon}}m_{t}+g_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg5.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
             <math id="alg5.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{t+1}=w_{t}-\operatorname{scale}\cdot\eta_{t}\operatorname{NS}(u_{t})-\eta_{t}\lambda w_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>scale</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>NS</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{t+1}=w_{t}-\operatorname{scale}\cdot\eta_{t}\operatorname{NS}(u_{t})-\eta_{t}\lambda w_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="alg5.l9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{scale}=0.2\sqrt{\max\{m,n\}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>scale</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>0.2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{scale}=0.2\sqrt{\max\{m,n\}}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="alg5.l9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times n}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg5.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
           <span id="alg5.l10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg5.l10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
</div>
</figure>
<figure id="alg6" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 6</span> </span> SOAP</figcaption>
<div id="alg6.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg6.l0" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg6.l0.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">0:</span></span>
            
            
           <math id="alg6.l0.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta,\beta_{v},\beta_{\mathrm{shampoo}},k,\epsilon,\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>shampoo</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta,\beta_{v},\beta_{\mathrm{shampoo}},k,\epsilon,\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg6.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
           Initialize state: <math id="alg6.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg6.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v=0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg6.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L=0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg6.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R=0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg6.l1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{l}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg6.l1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg6.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
           <span id="alg6.l2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg6.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1,2,\dots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1,2,\dots</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg6.l2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg6.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
            <span id="alg6.l3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">For weights in Output, Embedding, and Norm layers:</span>

</div>
<div id="alg6.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
             Update using AdamW with hyper-parameters <math id="alg6.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg6.l4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg6.l4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg6.l4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg6.l4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg6.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
            <span id="alg6.l5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <span id="alg6.l5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">weight matrices in transformer layers:</span> <span id="alg6.l5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg6.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
             Compute stochastic gradient <math id="alg6.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> at current parameters <math id="alg6.l6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg6.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
             <math id="alg6.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle G_{t}^{\text{rot}}=Q_{l}^{\top}G_{t}Q_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mi>t</mi><mtext>rot</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>l</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle G_{t}^{\text{rot}}=Q_{l}^{\top}G_{t}Q_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg6.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
             <math id="alg6.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{t}=\theta M_{t-1}+(1-\theta)G_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{t}=\theta M_{t-1}+(1-\theta)G_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg6.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
             <math id="alg6.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{t}=\beta_{v}V_{t-1}+(1-\beta_{v})(G_{t}^{\text{rot}})^{\odot 2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mi>t</mi><mtext>rot</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{t}=\beta_{v}V_{t-1}+(1-\beta_{v})(G_{t}^{\text{rot}})^{\odot 2}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg6.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
             <math id="alg6.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle W_{t+1}=W_{t}-\eta_{t}Q_{l}\left(\frac{Q_{l}^{\top}M_{t}Q_{r}}{\sqrt{V_{t}}+\epsilon}\right)Q_{r}^{\top}-\eta_{t}\lambda W_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>l</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle W_{t+1}=W_{t}-\eta_{t}Q_{l}\left(\frac{Q_{l}^{\top}M_{t}Q_{r}}{\sqrt{V_{t}}+\epsilon}\right)Q_{r}^{\top}-\eta_{t}\lambda W_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg6.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
             <math id="alg6.l11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{t}=\beta_{\mathrm{shampoo}}L_{t-1}+(1-\beta_{\mathrm{shampoo}})G_{t}G_{t}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>shampoo</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>shampoo</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{t}=\beta_{\mathrm{shampoo}}L_{t-1}+(1-\beta_{\mathrm{shampoo}})G_{t}G_{t}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg6.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
             <math id="alg6.l12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{t}=\beta_{\mathrm{shampoo}}R_{t-1}+(1-\beta_{\mathrm{shampoo}})G_{t}^{\top}G_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>shampoo</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>shampoo</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{t}=\beta_{\mathrm{shampoo}}R_{t-1}+(1-\beta_{\mathrm{shampoo}})G_{t}^{\top}G_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg6.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
             <span id="alg6.l13.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <math id="alg6.l13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\bmod k=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>mod</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\bmod k=0</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg6.l13.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>



</div>
<div id="alg6.l14" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
              <math id="alg6.l14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{l}\leftarrow\text{QR}(L_{t}Q_{l})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext>QR</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{l}\leftarrow\text{QR}(L_{t}Q_{l})</annotation></semantics></math> {QR decomposition}

</div>
<div id="alg6.l15" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
              <math id="alg6.l15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{r}\leftarrow\text{QR}(R_{t}Q_{r})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext>QR</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{r}\leftarrow\text{QR}(R_{t}Q_{r})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg6.l16" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
             <span id="alg6.l16.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg6.l16.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span>
</div>
<div id="alg6.l17" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
            <span id="alg6.l17.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg6.l17.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg6.l18" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
           <span id="alg6.l18.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg6.l18.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
</div>
</figure>
<section id="A9.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">I.1 </span>Exact Preconditioner (Riemannian Metrics) Forms for Common Adaptive Optimizers</h3>

<div id="A9.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A9.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we analyze the implicit metric structure <math id="A9.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> induced by the preconditioner estimation (update) scheme for each parameter block, and compare the way in approximating <math id="A9.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{F}(w)=(\mathbb{E}[gg^{\top}])^{1/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{F}(w)=(\mathbb{E}[gg^{\top}])^{1/2}</annotation></semantics></math> in <a href="#S4.SS1" title="4.1 A Unified Discrete Formulation ‣ 4 A Unified Riemannian ODE Framework for Understanding Adaptive Algorithms ‣ Accelerating LLM Pre-Training through Flat-Direction Dynamics Enhancement" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A9.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A9.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A9.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times n}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the stochastic gradient in matrix form, and let <math id="A9.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g=\operatorname{vec}(G)\in\mathbb{R}^{mn}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>vec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g=\operatorname{vec}(G)\in\mathbb{R}^{mn}</annotation></semantics></math> be its vectorized counterpart. The Fisher-type metric <math id="A9.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{F}(w)=(\mathbb{E}[gg^{\top}])^{1/2}\in\mathbb{R}^{mn\times mn}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{F}(w)=(\mathbb{E}[gg^{\top}])^{1/2}\in\mathbb{R}^{mn\times mn}</annotation></semantics></math> is often referred to the Whitening metric <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yang and Laaksonen, 2008</a>; <a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">Frans et al., 2025</a>)</cite>, which has demonstrated efficient and stable performance in neural network training. Below, we demonstrate how practical inverse preconditioners <math id="A9.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> in common adaptive optimizers approximate their corresponding deterministic forms <math id="A9.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(w_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(w_{k})</annotation></semantics></math>, which in turn serve as approximations of <math id="A9.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{F}(w_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{F}(w_{k})</annotation></semantics></math>. Throughout, we utilize the identity <math id="A9.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{vec}(ABC)=(C^{\top}\otimes A)\operatorname{vec}(B)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>vec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>vec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{vec}(ABC)=(C^{\top}\otimes A)\operatorname{vec}(B)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A9.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">EMA-based Preconditioners.</h4>

<div id="A9.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A9.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">AdamW employs an Exponential Moving Average (EMA) to update its preconditioner <math id="A9.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{k}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>F</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{k}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> via <math id="A9.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{k}=\operatorname{diag}v_{k}^{1/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{k}=\operatorname{diag}v_{k}^{1/2}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A9.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{k}=\beta_{v}v_{k-1}+(1-\beta_{v})g_{k}\odot g_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{k}=\beta_{v}v_{k-1}+(1-\beta_{v})g_{k}\odot g_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> . This expands to <math id="A9.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{k}=(1-\beta_{v})\sum_{i=0}^{k}\beta_{v}^{k-i}g_{i}\odot g_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{k}=(1-\beta_{v})\sum_{i=0}^{k}\beta_{v}^{k-i}g_{i}\odot g_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A9.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{v}</annotation></semantics></math> is typically close to <math id="A9.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>.
Observing that <math id="A9.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-\beta_{v})\sum_{i=k-t}^{k}\beta_{v}^{k-i}\approx 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-\beta_{v})\sum_{i=k-t}^{k}\beta_{v}^{k-i}\approx 1</annotation></semantics></math> for a large window <math id="A9.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, and assuming that the stochastic gradients <math id="A9.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> are approximately independent samples while <math id="A9.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{F}(w)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{F}(w)</annotation></semantics></math> changes slowly with respect to <math id="A9.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math>, we can deduce that <math id="A9.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{k}^{1/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{k}^{1/2}</annotation></semantics></math> provides a stable and efficient approximation of <math id="A9.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F^{\operatorname{adam}}(w)=\operatorname{diag}\hat{F}(w)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mi>adam</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F^{\operatorname{adam}}(w)=\operatorname{diag}\hat{F}(w)</annotation></semantics></math>.
This approximation logic can directly extend to other optimizers that accumulate preconditioners via EMA, such as SOAP. Specifically, for SOAP, from <a href="#alg6" title="In Appendix I Some Common Adaptive Optimizers for LLM Pre-training ‣ Accelerating LLM Pre-Training through Flat-Direction Dynamics Enhancement" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> we have</p>
<table id="A9.E72" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A9.E72.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{k}=(Q_{r}\otimes Q_{l})\left(\operatorname{diag}\operatorname{vec}(V_{k})\right)^{\frac{1}{2}}(Q_{r}\otimes Q_{l})^{\top},\,\text{with }V_{k}=\beta_{v}V_{k-1}+(1-\beta_{v})(G_{k}^{\text{rot}})^{\odot 2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>vec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>with </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi><mtext>rot</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{k}=(Q_{r}\otimes Q_{l})\left(\operatorname{diag}\operatorname{vec}(V_{k})\right)^{\frac{1}{2}}(Q_{r}\otimes Q_{l})^{\top},\,\text{with }V_{k}=\beta_{v}V_{k-1}+(1-\beta_{v})(G_{k}^{\text{rot}})^{\odot 2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(72)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A9.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{l},Q_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{l},Q_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> are updated in a lazy fashion, and <math id="A9.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{k}^{\text{rot}}=Q_{l}^{\top}G_{k}Q_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi><mtext>rot</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>l</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{k}^{\text{rot}}=Q_{l}^{\top}G_{k}Q_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>. This gives</p>
<table id="A9.E73" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A9.E73.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F^{\operatorname{soap}}(w)=(Q_{r}\otimes Q_{l})\left(\operatorname{diag}\mathbb{E}[g_{\operatorname{rot}}g_{\operatorname{rot}}^{\top}]\right)^{\frac{1}{2}}(Q_{r}\otimes Q_{l})^{\top}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mi>soap</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>rot</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>rot</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F^{\operatorname{soap}}(w)=(Q_{r}\otimes Q_{l})\left(\operatorname{diag}\mathbb{E}[g_{\operatorname{rot}}g_{\operatorname{rot}}^{\top}]\right)^{\frac{1}{2}}(Q_{r}\otimes Q_{l})^{\top},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(73)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A9.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{l}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A9.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> are the eigenvectors of <math id="A9.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[GG^{\top}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[GG^{\top}]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A9.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[G^{\top}G]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[G^{\top}G]</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively, and <math id="A9.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\operatorname{rot}}=\operatorname{vec}(Q_{l}^{\top}GQ_{r})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>rot</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>vec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>l</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\operatorname{rot}}=\operatorname{vec}(Q_{l}^{\top}GQ_{r})</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, <math id="A9.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F^{\operatorname{soap}}(w)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mi>soap</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F^{\operatorname{soap}}(w)</annotation></semantics></math> approximates <math id="A9.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{F}(w)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{F}(w)</annotation></semantics></math> via a structured, two-sided Kronecker factorization.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A9.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Momentum-based Preconditioners.</h4>

<div id="A9.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A9.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We take Muon as a representative example. At the <math id="A9.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-th iteration, the momentum is updated as <math id="A9.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{k}=\theta_{\operatorname{muon}}M_{k-1}+G_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>muon</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{k}=\theta_{\operatorname{muon}}M_{k-1}+G_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A9.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{k}\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{k}\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times n}</annotation></semantics></math> (assuming <math id="A9.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\geq n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\geq n</annotation></semantics></math>). We have <math id="A9.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{k}=(M_{k}^{\top}M_{k})^{1/2}\otimes I_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{k}=(M_{k}^{\top}M_{k})^{1/2}\otimes I_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> (or replacing <math id="A9.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> with its Nesterov-accelerated version). Expanding this recurrence yields <math id="A9.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{k}=\sum_{i=0}^{k}\theta_{\operatorname{muon}}^{k-i}G_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>muon</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{k}=\sum_{i=0}^{k}\theta_{\operatorname{muon}}^{k-i}G_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Analyzing the second moment, we have:</p>
<table id="A9.E74" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A9.E74.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[M_{k}^{\top}M_{k}]=\sum_{i,j\leq k}\theta_{\operatorname{muon}}^{2k-(i+j)}\mathbb{E}[G_{i}^{\top}G_{j}]\approx\sum_{i=0}^{k}\theta_{\operatorname{muon}}^{2(k-i)}\mathbb{E}[G_{i}^{\top}G_{i}]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>muon</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≈</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></munderover><mrow><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>muon</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[M_{k}^{\top}M_{k}]=\sum_{i,j\leq k}\theta_{\operatorname{muon}}^{2k-(i+j)}\mathbb{E}[G_{i}^{\top}G_{j}]\approx\sum_{i=0}^{k}\theta_{\operatorname{muon}}^{2(k-i)}\mathbb{E}[G_{i}^{\top}G_{i}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(74)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Here, we assume that in the middle to late stages of training, the deterministic gradient component is negligible compared to the stochastic noise (or second moment magnitude), and that gradient noise is approximately independent across different steps <math id="A9.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i,j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i,j</annotation></semantics></math> (<math id="A9.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\neq j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\neq j</annotation></semantics></math>).
Applying the same EMA perspective as used for AdamW, <math id="A9.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{k}^{\top}M_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{k}^{\top}M_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> serves as a stable estimator of <math id="A9.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{1-\theta_{\operatorname{muon}}^{2}}\mathbb{E}[G^{\top}G]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>muon</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{1-\theta_{\operatorname{muon}}^{2}}\mathbb{E}[G^{\top}G]</annotation></semantics></math>. Similarly, for the Nesterov-corrected momentum <math id="A9.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{M}_{k}=M_{k}+G_{k}/(1-\theta_{\operatorname{muon}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>muon</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{M}_{k}=M_{k}+G_{k}/(1-\theta_{\operatorname{muon}})</annotation></semantics></math>, we can similarly get that <math id="A9.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{M}_{k}^{\top}\widetilde{M}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{M}_{k}^{\top}\widetilde{M}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> approximates <math id="A9.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\mathbb{E}[G^{\top}G]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\mathbb{E}[G^{\top}G]</annotation></semantics></math> for some constant scaling factor <math id="A9.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>.
Consequently, the implicit metric for Muon can be characterized as <math id="A9.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F^{\operatorname{muon}}(w)\propto(\mathbb{E}[G^{\top}G])^{\frac{1}{2}}\otimes I_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mi>muon</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∝</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F^{\operatorname{muon}}(w)\propto(\mathbb{E}[G^{\top}G])^{\frac{1}{2}}\otimes I_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>, representing a single-sided Kronecker-factored approximation of <math id="A9.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{F}(w)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{F}(w)</annotation></semantics></math>.
This derivation extends naturally to element-wise operations on momentum; for instance, Lion’s update rule implies a metric <math id="A9.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F^{\operatorname{lion}}(w)\propto\operatorname{diag}(\hat{F}(w))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mi>lion</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F^{\operatorname{lion}}(w)\propto\operatorname{diag}(\hat{F}(w))</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A10" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix J </span>Proof</h2>

<section id="A10.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Notations</h4>

<div id="A10.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A10.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">A map is said to be smooth if it is infinitely differentiable. For notational brevity, we define <math id="A10.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{s}(w)=P_{s}(w)F(w)P_{s}(w)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{s}(w)=P_{s}(w)F(w)P_{s}(w)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A10.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{f}(w)=P_{f}(w)F(w)P_{f}(w)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{f}(w)=P_{f}(w)F(w)P_{f}(w)</annotation></semantics></math> and the corresponding pseudo inverse <math id="A10.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{s}^{\dagger}(w)=P_{s}(w)F^{-1}(w)P_{s}(w)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>F</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{s}^{\dagger}(w)=P_{s}(w)F^{-1}(w)P_{s}(w)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A10.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{f}^{\dagger}(w)=P_{f}(w)F^{-1}(w)P_{f}(w)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>F</mi><mi>f</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{f}^{\dagger}(w)=P_{f}(w)F^{-1}(w)P_{f}(w)</annotation></semantics></math>. Denote <math id="A10.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa_{F_{s}}:=\rho/\lambda_{F_{s}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{F_{s}}:=\rho/\lambda_{F_{s}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A10.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa_{F}:=\rho/\lambda_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{F}:=\rho/\lambda_{F}</annotation></semantics></math>. The full version of Assumption <a href="#S7.Thmtheorem2" title="Assumption 7.2 (Regularity, Smoothness and Conservation). ‣ 7 Theoretical Analysis to Training Dynamics ‣ Accelerating LLM Pre-Training through Flat-Direction Dynamics Enhancement" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.2</span></a>.<a href="#S7.I1.i2" title="Item 2 ‣ Assumption 7.2 (Regularity, Smoothness and Conservation). ‣ 7 Theoretical Analysis to Training Dynamics ‣ Accelerating LLM Pre-Training through Flat-Direction Dynamics Enhancement" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> concerning the operator norm bounds on <math id="A10.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla P_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla P_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A10.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla F</annotation></semantics></math> is as follows. For any <math id="A10.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u,v,w\in\mathbb{R}^{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u,v,w\in\mathbb{R}^{p}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="A10.E75" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A10.E75X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.E75X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\nabla P_{s}(w)[u]v\|_{F(w)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\nabla P_{s}(w)[u]v\|_{F(w)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.E75X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{\delta}{G}\|u\|_{F(w)}\|v\|_{F(w)}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>δ</mi><mi>G</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{\delta}{G}\|u\|_{F(w)}\|v\|_{F(w)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(75)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A10.E75Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.E75Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\nabla F(w)[u]v\|_{F^{-1}(w)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\nabla F(w)[u]v\|_{F^{-1}(w)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.E75Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{\delta_{F}}{G}\|u\|_{F(w)}\|v\|_{F(w)}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mi>G</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{\delta_{F}}{G}\|u\|_{F(w)}\|v\|_{F(w)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A10.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">J.1 </span>Landscape Analysis</h3>

<div id="A10.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A10.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this subsection we mainly focus on properties of <math id="A10.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A10.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A10.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A10.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma J.1</span></span><span id="A10.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A10.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A10.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose that Assumptions <a href="#S7.Thmtheorem2" title="Assumption 7.2 (Regularity, Smoothness and Conservation). ‣ 7 Theoretical Analysis to Training Dynamics ‣ Accelerating LLM Pre-Training through Flat-Direction Dynamics Enhancement" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.2</span></a> holds. Define <math id="A10.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{F_{s}}=2\delta+\delta_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{F_{s}}=2\delta+\delta_{F}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then we have</span></p>
<table id="A10.E76" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A10.E76.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max\{\|\nabla F_{s}^{{\dagger}}(w)[u]v\|_{F(w)},\|\nabla F_{f}^{{\dagger}}(w)[u]v\|_{F(w)}\}\leq\frac{\delta_{F_{s}}}{G}\|u\|_{F(w)}\|v\|_{F^{-1}(w)}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msubsup><mi>F</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msubsup><mi>F</mi><mi>f</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>δ</mi><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></msub><mi>G</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max\{\|\nabla F_{s}^{{\dagger}}(w)[u]v\|_{F(w)},\|\nabla F_{f}^{{\dagger}}(w)[u]v\|_{F(w)}\}\leq\frac{\delta_{F_{s}}}{G}\|u\|_{F(w)}\|v\|_{F^{-1}(w)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(76)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A10.E77" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A10.E77.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max\{\|\nabla F_{s}(w)[u]v\|_{F(w)},\|\nabla F_{f}(w)[u]v\|_{F(w)}\}\leq\frac{\delta_{F_{f}}}{G}\|u\|_{F(w)}\|v\|_{F(w)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>δ</mi><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></msub><mi>G</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max\{\|\nabla F_{s}(w)[u]v\|_{F(w)},\|\nabla F_{f}(w)[u]v\|_{F(w)}\}\leq\frac{\delta_{F_{f}}}{G}\|u\|_{F(w)}\|v\|_{F(w)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(77)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A10.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A10.Thmtheorem1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A10.Thmtheorem1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.Thmtheorem1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">By (<a href="#A10.E75" title="Equation 75 ‣ Notations ‣ Appendix J Proof ‣ Accelerating LLM Pre-Training through Flat-Direction Dynamics Enhancement" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">75</span></a>), we have</span></p>
<table id="A10.E78" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A10.E78X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.E78X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle v^{\top}\nabla(P_{s}F^{-1}P_{s})(w)[u]v=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub><mi>F</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>P</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle v^{\top}\nabla(P_{s}F^{-1}P_{s})(w)[u]v=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.E78X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 2v^{\top}\nabla P_{s}(w)[u]F^{-1}(w)P_{s}(w)v+v^{\top}P_{s}(w)\nabla(F^{-1})(w)[u]P_{s}(w)v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>v</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>P</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mi>F</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>P</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>v</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>P</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>∇</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>F</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mi>P</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 2v^{\top}\nabla P_{s}(w)[u]F^{-1}(w)P_{s}(w)v+v^{\top}P_{s}(w)\nabla(F^{-1})(w)[u]P_{s}(w)v</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="4" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(78)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A10.E78Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.E78Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.E78Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 2\|v\|_{F(w)^{-1}}\|\nabla P_{s}(w)[u]F(w)^{-1}P_{s}(w)v\|_{F(w)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 2\|v\|_{F(w)^{-1}}\|\nabla P_{s}(w)[u]F(w)^{-1}P_{s}(w)v\|_{F(w)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A10.E78Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.E78Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\|P_{s}(w)F(w)^{-1}v\|_{F(w)}\|\nabla F(w)[u]F(w)^{-1}P_{s}(w)v\|_{F(w)^{-1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\|P_{s}(w)F(w)^{-1}v\|_{F(w)}\|\nabla F(w)[u]F(w)^{-1